hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"12001","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us, Said ibn Anbasah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is unlawful by suckling is what is unlawful by lineage."
"12002","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The wife of Thabit came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: By Allah, I find no fault in him in character or religion, but I dislike disbelief after Islam; he said: Will you return his garden to him? She said: Yes; he said: O Thabit, accept the garden and divorce her with one divorce."
"12003","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: He used to dislike eating game that had spent the night away from its hunter."
"12004","Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wakii narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: married Maymunah while he was in ihram."
"12005","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Khalid, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"12006","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had cupping done while in ihram."
"12007","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is none among people more generous to me in favor of family or wealth than Abu Bakr, and had I taken an intimate friend, I would have taken him, but it is the brotherhood of Islam, or of faith."
"12008","Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Naqid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Razi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Tammam narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that Ali ibn Abi Talib proposed the daughter of Abu Jahl, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you marry her, return our daughter to us."
"12009","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of Badr while in his dome: O Allah, I implore You by Your covenant and Your promise; O Allah, if You will, You will not be worshipped after today; and Abu Bakr took his hand and said: Enough, O Messenger of Allah, you have entreated your Lord insistently, while he was in armor; so he went out saying: The multitude will be defeated and turn their backs; rather the Hour is their appointment, and the Hour is more disastrous and more bitter."
"12010","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: forbade the jallalah animal and the tied-up living target, and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin."
"12011","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade drinking from the mouth of the waterskin, and breathing into the vessel."
"12012","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Allaf narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Khattab ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakrah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Were it not that dogs are a community among communities, I would have ordered the killing of every jet-black dog; so kill the helpful one among dogs, for it is the accursed one among the jinn."
"12013","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Bakr ibn al-Rabi ibn Muslim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humran narrated to us, Uthman ibn Sad al-Makki narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he did not meet the enemy at the start of the day, delayed until the wind blew and until the times of prayers, and he used to say: O Allah, by You I attack, and by You I move about, and there is no power and no strength except by Allah."
"12014","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Ali ibn Abd Allah al-Farghani Tughk narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Sad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, when I eat meat, I become aroused for women, and desire overtakes me, so I forbade meat upon myself; so Allah, Exalted is He, sent down: O you who believe, do not forbid the good things Allah has made lawful for you, and do not transgress; indeed Allah does not love transgressors, and eat of what Allah has provided you, lawful and good."
"12015","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn Akhram narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Uthman ibn Murrah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade naqir, muzaffat, dubba, jarr and hantam."
"12016","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Uthman ibn Murrah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: al-Abbas was traveling with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon a camel he had branded on its face with fire, so he said: What is this brand, O Abbas? He said: A brand we used to brand in the pre-Islamic time; so he said: Do not brand by burning."
"12017","Al-Hasan ibn Alawayh al-Qattan narrated to us, Abbad ibn Musa al-Khuttalli narrated to us, Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Israil, from Uthman al-Shahham, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a blind man had an umm walad who insulted the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and often reviled him; so he forbade her but she did not stop, and he rebuked her but she was not rebuked; then one night she mentioned the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he could not bear it, so he stood to the dagger, placed it in her belly, then leaned upon it until he killed her; so her two children woke between her legs stained with blood; so he mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; so he stood, gathered the people, then said: I adjure by Allah a man upon whom there is a right who did what he did to stand; so the blind man came wailing and said: I am, by Allah, O Prophet of Allah, her owner, and she is my umm walad, and I have from her two like pearls, and she was gentle and kind to me, but she used to mention you and insult you, so I forbade her but she did not stop, and I rebuked her but she was not rebuked; then last night she mentioned you and reviled you, so I could not bear it, so I stood to the dagger, placed it in her belly, then leaned upon it until I killed her; so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I bear witness that her blood is void."
"12018","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Uthman al-Shahham, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Our wine in those days was fadikh date-wine, and it was forbidden on the day it was forbidden, and it was only your fadikh."
"12019","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ramli narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Khattab ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakrah narrated to us, Hanzalah al-Sadusi narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed qunut in the Fajr prayer."
"12020","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed effeminate men and masculinized women."
"12021","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed effeminate men and masculinized women."
"12022","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed effeminate men and masculinized women, and expelled so-and-so."
"12023","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Expel effeminate men from your houses; he said: And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, expelled an effeminate man, and Umar expelled an effeminate man."
"12024","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Umar ibn Rashid, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The blood-money of the mukatab is according to what has been freed of him, the blood-money of the freeman, and according to what remains enslaved of him, the blood-money of the slave."
"12025","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bishr al-Hariri narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ruled regarding the mukatab that blood-money be paid according to what has been freed of him as the blood-money of the freeman."
"12026","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a mukatab was raised to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: He is paid for what he has paid of his contract as the blood-money of the freeman, and what he has not paid as the blood-money of the slave."
"12027","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman al-Nashiti narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The blood-money of the mukatab is according to what has been freed of him as the blood-money of the freeman, and what remains enslaved of him as the blood-money of the owned slave."
"12028","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, I think from Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever vows to slaughter himself or his child should slaughter a ram; then he recited: You have indeed in the Messenger of Allah an excellent example."
"12029","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, both saying: Shihab ibn Abbad narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated to us, from Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling animals on credit."
"12030","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abu Salih Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, both saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Said ibn Yusuf, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Treat your children equally in giving, for had I preferred anyone, I would have preferred women."
"12031","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abbad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Said ibn Yusuf, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, changed his ihram garment at al-Tanim while in ihram."
"12032","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Abi al-Asbat, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abi Salamah, from Abi Hurayrah, and Hatim, from Abi al-Asbat, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was proposed to for one of his daughters, he came to the curtain and said: So-and-so proposes to so-and-so; if she struck the wall, he did not marry her off, and if she did not strike the wall, he married her off."
"12033","Musa ibn Harun, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, all saying: Said ibn Zunbur narrated to us, Abd al-Majid ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he married Fatimah off, said: Give her your Hutami armor."
"12034","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Juta al-Sanani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Malik al-Dhimari narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, annulled the marriage of a virgin and a previously married woman whom their father married off while they were unwilling."
"12035","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu Awn al-Ziyadi narrated to us, Abu Izzah al-Dabbagh narrated to us, from Abu Yazid al-Madini, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had cupping done and gave the cupper his wage; the name of Abu Izzah is al-Hakam ibn Tahman."
"12036","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu Awn al-Ziyadi narrated, Abu Azzah al-Dabbagh narrated, from Abu Yazid al-Madani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: a man of the Ansar had two breeding camels that became unruly, so he put them in a walled garden and shut the door on them, then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sitting with a group of the Ansar and said: O Prophet of Allah, I have come for a need; my two camels became unruly so I put them in a garden and shut the door, and I wish you would supplicate for me that Allah subdue them for me. He said to his Companions: Rise with us. He went to the door and said: Open. He opened the door, and one camel was near the door; when it saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) it prostrated to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me something with which to tie its head and give you control over it. He brought a halter, so he tied its head and gave him control over it. Then they walked to the far end of the garden to the other camel, and when it saw him it fell prostrate to him. He said to the man: Bring me something with which to tie its head. So he tied its head and gave him control over it, and said: Go, for they will not disobey you. When the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, they said: O Messenger of Allah, these two camels, which have no reason, prostrated to you, shall we not prostrate to you? He said: I do not command anyone to prostrate to anyone, and if I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone I would have commanded the wife to prostrate to her husband."
"12037","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Said ibn Yaqub al-Talqani narrated (ha), and Ahmad ibn Anbar al-Misri narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated, both said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Abu Yazid al-Madani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep to the first row, and keep to the right side, and beware of the row between the pillars."
"12038","Muhammad ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Abu Yazid al-Madani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in some prayers and was silent in some prayers, so we recite in what the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in, and we are silent in what he was silent in. It was said to him: Perhaps the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited to himself. He became angry and said: Is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to be accused? Is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to be accused?"
"12039","Yahya ibn Mansur Abu Said al-Harawi narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Nasr narrated, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Yahya ibn Bishr, that he heard Ikrimah narrating, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he fixed Dhul-Hulayfah for the people of Madinah, Juhfah for the people of Syria, and Yalamlam for the people of Yemen."
"12040","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Abu Zufar Abd al-Salam ibn Mutahhar narrated, Nafi Abu Hurmuz narrated, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Three men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The first said: Peace upon you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: And upon you, and the mercy of Allah. The second came and said: Peace upon you and the mercy of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: And upon you, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. The third came and said: Peace upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: And upon you. The father of the youth was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, you added for so-and-so and so-and-so but added nothing for my son. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We found no addition left, so we returned to him the like of what he said."
"12041","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Abi al-Hasna al-Sarakhsi narrated, Abu al-Sabbah Abd al-Ghafur ibn Said al-Ansari al-Wasiti narrated, from Abu Hashim al-Rummani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: He who plunders is not of us. And he said: There is no shighar in Islam. And shighar is that two women be married, one in exchange for the other, without a dowry."
"12042","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated, Abd al-Ghafur narrated, from Abu Hashim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: Circumcision is a sunnah for men and an honor for women."
"12043","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated, Abd al-Ghafur narrated, from Abu Hashim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, I do not think but that he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Prayer at the dwellings."
"12044","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated, Abd al-Ghafur narrated, from Abu Hashim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man seeks a need and Allah turns it away from him for what is better for him, then he accuses people, wronging them, saying: Who has satiated me?"
"12045","Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Ismail al-Razi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Farra narrated, Abdullah ibn Ismah narrated, from Abu al-Sabbah, from Abu Hashim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Three have no reckoning for what they eat if it is lawful: the fasting person, the one taking the pre-dawn meal, and the one stationed in the path of Allah."
"12046","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh al-Himsi narrated, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Abu al-Sabbah Abd al-Ghafur al-Ansari, from Abu Hashim al-Rummani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are about to see the devils of mankind; one of them hears the hadith and spreads it on behalf of another, turning people away from hearing it from its narrator who narrates it."
"12047","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Qirmiti al-Adawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Mawardi narrated, Ziyad ibn Sahl narrated, Bishr ibn Ali narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, aided me with the fiercest of the Arabs in tongues and arms: Banu Qaylah, al-Aws and al-Khazraj."
"12048","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Jafar ibn Sulayman ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated, my father narrated to me, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, is there any supplication that is not rejected? He said: Yes; you say: I ask You by Your Highest, Mightiest, Most Majestic, Most Noble Name."
"12049","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated, my father narrated, Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated, from Amr ibn Hurmuz, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Aishah bathed from a single vessel in a state of major impurity, and both performed ablution for prayer."
"12050","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri informed, Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti narrated, from Isa ibn Hilal al-Sadusi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels do not attend with good the one in major impurity, nor the one smeared with saffron perfume, until they both bathe."
"12051","Al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Duri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Amr Abu Sufyan al-Ghanawi narrated, Hafs ibn Umar al-Adani narrated, Musa ibn Sad narrated, from Maymun al-Qannad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Allah gave speech to Musa, close friendship to Ibrahim, and vision to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12052","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated, Khalid ibn Abdullah al-Wasiti narrated, from Aban ibn Abi Ayyash, from Zayd ibn Subayh, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He who performs ablution after the ritual bath is not of us."
"12053","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated, Umar ibn Harun narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Isa al-Thaqafi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the news of the death of Jafar ibn Abi Talib came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Asma bint Umays and placed Abdullah and Muhammad, the two sons of Jafar, on his thigh, then said: Jibril informed me that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, granted Jafar martyrdom, and that he has two wings with which he flies with the angels in Paradise. Then he said: O Allah, succeed Jafar among his offspring."
"12054","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated, Shabib ibn Bishr informed, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, about: And your turning among those who prostrate. He said: From prophet to prophet until you were brought forth a prophet."
"12055","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated, Abu Asim narrated, from Shabib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the privy, then came out and found a covered brass vessel. He said: Who did this? Abdullah said: I. He said: O Allah, teach him the interpretation of the Quran."
"12056","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah ibn Yazid al-Harrani narrated, my father narrated to me, Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Tawus and Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Dubaaah: Perform Hajj and stipulate, saying: My release is where You detain me."
"12057","Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, from Jafar ibn Rabiah (ha), and Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, al-Layth narrated to me, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting."
"12058","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Shaybah al-Juddi narrated, Sharik narrated, from Khusayf, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to give half a dinar in charity."
"12059","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Khattab ibn al-Qasim narrated, from Khusayf, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he disliked combining a paternal aunt and a maternal aunt, and two paternal aunts and two maternal aunts, in marriage."
"12060","Sulayman ibn al-Muafa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Khattab ibn al-Qasim narrated, from Khusayf, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Aishah and Hafsah while they were both fasting, then he went out and returned while they were eating. He said: Were you not both fasting? They said: Yes, but this food was gifted to us and it pleased us, so we ate of it. He said: Fast a day in its place."
"12061","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, from Khusayf, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: This verse was revealed on the Day of Badr: And it is not for a prophet to misappropriate, concerning a red cloak lost on the Day of Badr; some people said: Perhaps the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: And it is not for a prophet to misappropriate."
"12062","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Layth narrated, al-Ashjai narrated, from Sufyan, from Khusayf, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, about: And it is not for a prophet to misappropriate. He said: Concerning a red cloak they lost on the Day of Badr; they said: He took it, so there was revealed: And it is not for a prophet to misappropriate."
"12063","Al-Fadl ibn Marwan al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abu Mamar al-Qatii narrated, Marwan ibn Shuja narrated, from Khusayf, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about the woman in postnatal bleeding: She bathes, then enters ihram and performs all the rites except the circumambulation of the House."
"12064","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated (ha), and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, both said: Attab ibn Bashir narrated, from Khusayf, from Mujahid and Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the poor came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: The rich fast as we fast and pray as we pray, and they have wealth with which they give charity and free slaves. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: When you pray, say: Glory be to Allah thirty-three times, and praise be to Allah thirty-three times, and Allah is Greatest thirty-four times."
"12065","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Harun ibn Maruf narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Khusayf, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, about: Indeed He who imposed the Quran upon you will surely return you to a place of return. He said: Your return is from Paradise."
"12066","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Yahya ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated (ha), and Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, both said: Abdullah ibn Lahiah narrated, from his brother Isa ibn Lahiah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When Surat al-Nisa was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no withholding after Surat al-Nisa."
"12067","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Nafi ibn Yazid informed, Uthman ibn Ata al-Khurasani narrated to us, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: A Day that will make children grey-haired. He said: That is the Day of Resurrection, and it is a Day on which Allah, Majestic His mention, will say to Adam: Rise and send forth from your offspring a delegation to the Fire. He will say: From how many, O Lord? He will say: From a thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine, and one will be saved. That weighed heavily on the Muslims, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when he saw that in their faces: The children of Adam are many, and Gog and Magog are of the children of Adam, and no man of them dies until a thousand men of his loins inherit him, and among them and their likes is a shield for you."
"12068","Ahmad ibn Anas ibn Malik al-Dimashqi, Abu Amir Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Nahwi al-Suri, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Dhakwan al-Dimashqi narrated, Irak ibn Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Subayh al-Murri narrated, from Uthman ibn Ata al-Khurasani, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was consoled for his daughter Ruqayyah, the wife of Uthman ibn Affan, he said: Praise be to Allah; the burial of daughters is among honorable deeds."
"12069","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi narrated, Abu Salih and Ikrimah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Ali ibn Abi Talib said: O Messenger of Allah, the Quran slips from my chest. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I teach you words by which Allah will benefit you and benefit whomever you teach? He said: Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. He said: Pray on Friday night four rakahs: recite in the first rakah the Opening of the Book and Yasin, in the second the Opening of the Book and Ha-Mim, the Smoke, in the third the Opening of the Book and Alif Lam Mim, the Revelation, the Prostration, and in the fourth the Opening of the Book and Tabarak, the Detailed. When you finish the tashahhud, praise Allah and extol Him, send blessings upon the prophets, seek forgiveness for the believers, then say: O Allah, have mercy on me by abandoning disobedience as long as You keep me alive, have mercy on me from burdening myself with what does not concern me, grant me good consideration of what pleases You of me. O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Possessor of majesty, honor, and might that cannot be attained, I ask You, O Allah, O Merciful, by Your majesty and the light of Your face, to bind my heart to love Your Book as You taught me, grant me to recite it in the manner that pleases You of me, and I ask You to illumine my sight by the Book, free my tongue by it, relieve my heart by it, expand my chest by it, employ my body by it, strengthen me for that and aid me in it, for none aids me in good but You, and none grants success in it but You. Do that for three, five, or seven Fridays; you will memorize it by Allah's permission, and a believer never errs in it. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after seven Fridays and told him of his memorization of the Quran and hadith. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A believer, by the Lord of the Kabah; teach Abu Hasan, teach Abu Hasan."
"12070","Ahmad ibn Shuayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Marwazi narrated, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated, from his father, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment; they took spoils, and among them was a man who said to them: I am not of them; I loved a woman and followed her, so let me look at her, then do what you wish. And there was a tall dark woman, so he said to her: Accept Islam, Hubaysh, before life runs out, in travel. She said: Yes, may I be sacrificed for you. He said: So they brought him forward and struck his neck. The woman came, fell upon him, sobbed once or twice, then died. When they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him the news, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Was there not among you a merciful man?"
"12071","Isa ibn al-Qasim al-Saydalani al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr ibn al-Hakam al-Naysaburi narrated, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated, my father narrated to me, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Abu Sufyan ibn Harb came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, I adjure you by Allah and kinship; we have eaten al-ilhiz, meaning fur and blood. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: And We seized them with punishment, but they did not humble themselves to their Lord nor supplicate."
"12072","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Said ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated, Abu Tumaylah narrated, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A thousand of Banu Sulaym witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of the Conquest of Makkah."
"12073","Ahmad ibn al-Khadir al-Khuzai al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdah al-Marwazi narrated, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated, my father narrated to me, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, about His saying: And fear a Day in which you will be returned to Allah, that it is the last verse revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12074","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr ibn al-Hakam narrated, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated, my father narrated to me, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah they were among the worst of people in measuring, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Woe to those who give short measure. So they measured well after that."
"12075","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abu al-Darda Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Munib narrated, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Kaysan narrated, my father narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from the campaign of Khaybar, there was revealed to him: When the help of Allah and the victory comes, to the end of the account. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ali ibn Abi Talib, O Fatimah, the help of Allah and the victory has come, and you see people entering Allah's religion in crowds, so glorify the praise of your Lord and seek His forgiveness; indeed He is ever Accepting of repentance, upon that there will be after me struggle among the believers. He said: For what do we fight believers who say: We believe? He said: Against innovating in the religion, when they act by opinion, and there is no opinion in the religion; religion is only from the Lord, His command and His prohibition. Ali said: O Messenger of Allah, what if a matter arises for which no Quran has come down and no sunnah of yours specifies it? He said: You make it consultation among the worshipping believers, and do not decide it by private opinion. Had I been appointing anyone, none would be worthier of it than you, for your precedence in Islam, your kinship to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), your marriage, mistress of believing women being with you, and before that Abu Talib's support of me, and the Quran was revealed while I was keen to honor him in his offspring."
"12076","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abdullah al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abu al-Darda Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Munib narrated, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Kaysan narrated to me, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Ali said: O Messenger of Allah, you said to me on the Day of Uhud when I was kept from martyrdom and those martyred were martyred: Martyrdom is behind you - how will your patience be when this is dyed from this, motioning with his hand to his beard and head. Ali said: As you explained, that is not among the occasions of patience, but it is among the occasions of glad tidings and honor."
"12077","Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Hammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kalbi narrated, al-Mubarak ibn Abi Hamzah al-Zubaydi narrated, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Sacrifice was enjoined upon me but not enjoined upon you, and I was commanded the forenoon prayer but you were not commanded it."
"12078","Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn Yazid al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated, Safwan ibn Amr narrated, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Abu Barzah al-Aslami was a soothsayer judging among the Jews in what they disputed to him; some Muslims disputed to him, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Have you not seen those who claim they believe in what was revealed to you and what was revealed before you, wishing to seek judgment from the taghut though they were commanded to disbelieve in it, to His saying: We intended only good."
"12079","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bahr al-Hujaymi narrated, Sulaym ibn Muslim al-Makki narrated, al-Nadr ibn Arabi narrated, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He who drinks in a vessel of gold only gulps the fire of Hell in his belly."
"12080","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Amr ibn Hisham Abu Umayyah al-Harrani narrated, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from Anbasah ibn Hubayrah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created one hundred mercies; one mercy of them He divided among creatures, and ninety-nine till the Day of Resurrection."
"12081","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, my father narrated (ha). And Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated, both said: Ibn Lahiah narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hassan, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The barefooted is more entitled to the front of the road than the shod."
"12082","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abu al-Darda Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Munib narrated, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Kaysan narrated, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he returned from the campaign of Tabuk and performed Umrah, when he descended from the pass of Usfan ordered his Companions to stay by the mountain path until I return to you. He went and stopped at his mother's grave and conversed with his Lord at length, then he wept and his weeping intensified, and they wept for his weeping and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wept in this place only because something unbearable has been introduced against his community. When they wept he rose and returned to them and said: What makes you weep? They said: O Prophet of Allah, we wept for your weeping; we said: perhaps something unbearable has been introduced against your community. He said: No, though part of it has occurred, but I stopped at my mother's grave and asked Allah to permit me to intercede for her on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah refused to permit me, so I pitied her, for she is my mother, and I wept. Then Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: And the seeking of forgiveness of Ibrahim for his father was only about a promise he had promised him, then when it became clear to him that he was an enemy to Allah he dissociated from him. So dissociate yourself from your mother as Ibrahim dissociated from his father. So I pitied her, for she is my mother, and I asked my Lord to lift four things from my community; He lifted two from them and refused to lift two from them. I asked my Lord to lift from them stoning from the sky, drowning from the earth, that He not clothe them in factions, and that He not make some taste the violence of others. So Allah lifted from them stoning from the sky and drowning from the earth, and Allah refused to lift two from them: killing and widespread killing. He turned aside to his mother's grave only because she was buried beneath such-and-such, and Usfan belonged to them."
"12083","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah narrated to me, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated, Abdullah ibn Kaysan narrated, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named the two prostrations of forgetfulness the two humiliators of Satan."
"12084","Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Aktham the judge narrated, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated, Abdullah ibn Kaysan narrated, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not pray toward a grave, and do not pray upon a grave."
"12085","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Said ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to me, Abu Tumaylah narrated, Nuaym ibn Said al-Abdi narrated, that Ikrimah narrated, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dug the Trench while his Companions had tied stones on their bellies from hunger. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, he said: Have you been directed to a man who will feed us a meal? A man said: Yes. He said: Then go ahead and lead us to him. They set out to the man, who was in the Trench working his share of it. His wife sent word: Come, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has come to us. The man came hurrying and said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you; he had a she-goat with its kid, so he leapt to it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The kid is behind us. So he slaughtered the kid, and the woman took her flour, kneaded it and baked it, the pot caught up, and she made tharid in her bowl and brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his finger in it and said: In the name of Allah, O Allah bless it; eat. They ate of it till they were full, and they ate only a third of it while two thirds remained. He sent off those ten who were with him, saying: Go and send to us your number. They went, and those other ten came in their place and ate of it till they were satiated. Then he stood and supplicated for the mistress of the house and blessed her and her household. Then they walked to the Trench and he said: Take us to Salman. There was a rock before him that had weakened him. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Leave me to be the first to strike it. He said: In the name of Allah, and struck it; a third of it fell as a flake. He said: Allah is Greatest, the palaces of Rome, by the Lord of the Kabah. Then he struck another and a flake fell. He said: Allah is Greatest, the palaces of Persia, by the Lord of the Kabah. At that the hypocrites said: We are digging a trench against ourselves while he promises us the palaces of Persia and Rome."
"12086","Miqsam from Ibn Abbas: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Shubah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting."
"12087","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, both said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated (ha), and Yusuf the judge narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, both said: Shubah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out in Ramadan at the time of the Conquest, fasting until he was at Qudayd, where he broke his fast, and his Companions broke their fast until they arrived at Makkah. The wording is that of Sulayman ibn Harb."
"12088","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Shuja narrated, Musab ibn Sallam narrated, from Shubah, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trotted the first three circuits from stone to stone in his Hajj and walked the four."
"12089","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in two white cloaks and a red cloak."
"12090","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated (ha), and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated, both from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gifted one hundred sacrificial camels, among them a camel of Abu Jahl ibn Hisham with a silver nose-ring."
"12091","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Muslims captured a man of the great polytheists, and he asked them to ransom him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them to sell for his carcass."
"12092","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) employed Arqam ibn Abi al-Arqam al-Zuhri over charity collection, and he enlisted Abu Rafi. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him. He said: O Abu Rafi, charity is forbidden to Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, and the freedman of a people is of themselves."
"12093","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that Abu Qatadah killed a slain man, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave Abu Qatadah and his spoils."
"12094","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with Jibril, peace be upon him, conversing with him, the horizon of the sky split. Jibril began to draw near the earth, swaying, and an angel appeared before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, Allah commands you to choose between a prophet servant or a king prophet. He said: Jibril signaled to me with his hand to be humble, so I knew he was advising me, and I said: A servant prophet. That angel ascended to the sky. I said: O Jibril, I had wanted to ask you about this, but what I saw of your state distracted me from the question; who is this, O Jibril? He said: This is Israfil; Allah created him, on the day He created him, before Him with his feet in rank, not raising his glance; between him and the Lord are seventy lights, none of which one nearly approaches but is burned. Before him is a tablet; when Allah, Mighty and Majestic, permits something in the heaven or the earth, that revelation rises and strikes his forehead, so he looks: if it is of my work he commands me with it, if of the work of Mikail he commands him with it, and if of the work of the angel of death he commands him with it. I said: O Jibril, what are you over? He said: Over the wind and the troops. I said: What is Mikail over? He said: Over vegetation and rain. I said: What is the angel of death over? He said: Over seizing souls. And I thought he descended only for the Hour, and what you saw of me was only fear of the Hour."
"12095","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Miqsam Abu al-Qasim, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he conquered Khaybar, stipulated for himself the land and every yellow and white, meaning gold and silver. The people of Khaybar said to him: We know the land best, so give it to us to work, with half the fruit for us and half for you. He mentioned that he gave them on that basis. When the time for cutting dates came, he sent Ibn Rawahah to them, who estimated the dates, which the people of Madinah call estimation. He said: In this is so much and so much. They said: You have exaggerated against us, O Ibn Rawahah. He said: The estimation of the dates is up to me; I will give you half of what I said. They said: This is the truth, and by it the heavens and the earth stand; we agree to take what you said."
"12096","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from Kathir ibn Abi Sulayman, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The number of the people of Badr was three hundred and thirteen."
"12097","Yahya ibn Mansur Abu Sad al-Harawi and Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, both said: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated, Ahmad ibn Ayyub informed, from Abu Hamzah, from Jabir, from Shibl ibn Ali, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What is below the ankles of the lower garment is in the Fire."
"12098","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, Hammad ibn al-Jad narrated, Qatadah narrated, al-Hakam ibn Utaybah narrated to me, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that a man came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and claimed he had fallen upon his wife while she was menstruating, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to give a dinar in charity, and if he did not find, then half a dinar."
"12099","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Shubah, Abd al-Hakam narrated to me, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), about one who comes to his wife while she is menstruating: he gives a dinar or half a dinar in charity."
"12100","Abu Hanifah Muhammad ibn Hanifah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sini narrated, Nasr ibn Hammad Abu al-Harith al-Warraq narrated, Shubah narrated, from al-Suddi, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over the slain of Badr and said: May Allah recompense you from me, O band, with evil; you betrayed me, the trustworthy, and belied me, the truthful. Then he turned to Abu Jahl ibn Hisham and said: This one was more insolent toward Allah than Pharaoh; Pharaoh, when he was certain of destruction, declared Allah One, while this one, when he was certain of death, called upon al-Lat and al-Uzza."
"12101","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made peace with the people of Khaybar for every yellow and white and everything except their lives and offspring. He said: Al-Rabi and Kinanah, the two sons of Abi al-Huqayq, were brought, one of them a bridegroom to Safiyyah bint Huyayy. He said: Where are your vessels that were borrowed at the weddings of Madinah? He said: You expelled and exiled us so we spent them. He said: Consider what you say, for if you conceal from me I will thereby deem your blood and offspring lawful. He said: He called a man of the Ansar and said: Go to such-and-such a place; look at a small palm with a patch on its top, remove that patch, take out those vessels and bring them to me. He went and brought them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought them forward and struck their necks, and sent for their offspring. Safiyyah was brought as a bride, so he ordered Bilal, who took her to the house of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Bilal went and passed by her husband and his brother while they were both slain. When he returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Glory be to Allah, what did you mean, O Bilal, by a young virgin girl to pass her by two slain men showing them to her; have you no mercy? He said: I wanted to burn her inside. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and spent the night with her, and Abu Ayyub came with his sword and sat beside the tent. He said: If I heard alarm or anything suspicious I would be near the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out at Bilal's call to prayer. He said: Who is this? He said: I am Abu Ayyub. He said: What is the matter with you here at this hour? He said: O Messenger of Allah, you entered with a young virgin girl whose husband and brother you had killed, so I feared for you; I said: I will be near the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: May Allah have mercy on you, Abu Ayyub, three times. People spoke much about her; one saying: his concubine, another saying: his wife. At departure they said: Look at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); if he veils her she is his wife, and if he does not veil her she is his concubine. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought her out and veiled her, placed his knee, and she placed her knee on his thigh and mounted. He had earlier offered her to take her as a concubine, or free her, or marry her. She said: No, rather free me and marry me. So he did (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12102","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was kept from the Asr prayer till the sun set, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They kept us from the middle prayer; may Allah fill their graves and houses with fire."
"12103","Isa ibn Muhammad al-Simsar al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid informed, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House on a camel and touched the Corner with his curved stick."
"12104","Isa ibn Muhammad al-Simsar al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid informed, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gifted one hundred sacrificial camels, slaughtered sixty of them himself, ordered a man of his Companions who slaughtered forty of them, ordered him to take a piece of each camel strung on a cord cooked in a pot, and he ate of it and sipped."
"12105","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father narrated to me, Ibn Abi Layla narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Hands are not raised except in seven places: when opening the prayer, when entering the Sacred Mosque looking at the House, when standing on al-Safa, when standing on al-Marwah, when standing with the people on the evening of Arafah and at Muzdalifah, and the two stations when stoning the jamrah."
"12106","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father narrated, Ibn Abi Layla narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me from Muzdalifah to Mina among the weak of his household, taking each one's upper arm and saying: Do not stone the jamrah until the sun rises."
"12107","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Yazid al-Tahhan narrated, Aidh ibn Habib narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled in the month of Ramadan; his Companions complained of thirst, so he called for water, drank, some people broke their fast and some fasted, and neither group faulted what its fellows did."
"12108","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father narrated to me, Ibn Abi Layla narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, about His saying: And they ask you what they spend; say: Pardon. He said: Surplus beyond one's dependents."
"12109","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father narrated to me, Ibn Abi Layla narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: And the Day the enemies of Allah are gathered to the Fire, driven. He said: Their first is held back for their last."
"12110","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions came in the truce between him and the polytheists, the polytheists being at the door of al-Nadwah near al-Hijr, having said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions were afflicted with strain and emaciation. When they touched the Stone, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: They have said you are afflicted with strain and emaciation, so trot the three circuits that they may see you have strength. When they touched the Stone they lifted their feet and trotted. Some said to others: Do they not claim they are strained and emaciated; they are not content with walking till they run."
"12111","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) moved his weak household from Muzdalifah by night, then came to us one by one striking our thighs; I was among those whose thigh he struck, then said: O my son, do not stone the jamrat al-Aqabah until the sun rises."
"12112","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu Muawiyah narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed, on the Day of Taif, those of the slaves of the polytheists who came out to him."
"12113","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House on his mount and touched the Corner with his curved stick, then came to the watering place while his cousins were drawing from it; he asked for a drink, the bucket was lifted to him, he drank of it and said: Were it not that people would reckon and take it as a rite, fighting you over it, I would have drawn with you. Then he came to al-Safa and al-Marwah and trotted between them on his mount."
"12114","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) directed Abdullah ibn Rawahah al-Ansari, Jafar ibn Abi Talib, and Zayd ibn Harithah. Abdullah ibn Rawahah stayed back. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What kept you back? He said: Friday, O Messenger of Allah; I pray Friday then go. He said: A morning going or an evening return in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it. So he went forth departing."
"12115","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a slain woman on the Day of the Trench and said: Who killed her? A man said: I, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Why? He said: She wrestled my sword from me. He was silent."
"12116","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The number of the people of Badr was three hundred and thirteen; the Emigrants were over sixty men, the Ansar two hundred and thirty-six men. The bearer of the Emigrants' banner was Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with them, and the bearer of the Ansar's banner was Sad ibn Ubadah, may Allah be pleased with them."
"12117","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ammar ibn Abi Malik al-Janbi narrated, my father narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The mark of the angels on the Day of Badr was white turbans let down to their backs, and on the Day of Hunayn red turbans. The angels did not fight on any day except the Day of Badr; rather they were numbers and reinforcement, not striking."
"12118","Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, Ammar ibn Abi Malik al-Janbi narrated, my father narrated, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped in Ramadan and fainted, and for that he disliked it."
"12119","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah and Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Amiri narrated to us, both said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting and in ihram."
"12120","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi narrated, Umar ibn Ali narrated, from Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned the jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice, then slaughtered, then shaved."
"12121","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my uncle Abu Bakr narrated, Aidh ibn Habib narrated, from Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Day of Badr was the twenty-seventh of Ramadan."
"12122","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my uncle Abu Bakr narrated, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated, from Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He who has intercourse with a pregnant woman is not of us."
"12123","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated, Sad ibn al-Salt narrated, from Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach on Friday standing, then sit, then stand and preach."
"12124","Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, my father narrated, Sad ibn al-Salt narrated, from Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that two slaves came out on the Day of Taif while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was besieging them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed them."
"12125","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my uncle al-Qasim narrated, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated, from Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to Maymunah bint al-Harith; she placed her affair with al-Abbas, who married her to him."
"12126","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my uncle al-Qasim narrated to me, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated, Sharik narrated, from Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib and Hanzalah ibn al-Rahib were struck, both being in major impurity, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw the angels washing them."
"12127","Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Maymun narrated, Musab ibn Sallam narrated, from Sad ibn Tarif, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that he was asked about His saying: The month of Ramadan in which the Quran was revealed, and His saying: Indeed We sent it down on a blessed night. He said: It was sent down in Ramadan, on the Night of Decree, on a blessed night, all at once, then sent down at the stations of the stars piecemeal through months and days."
"12128","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muti al-Shaybani narrated, Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated, from his father, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah returned from Uhud, the women of the Ansar wept for their martyrs; that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: But Hamzah has no weepers. The Ansar returned and said to their women: Weep for none till you eulogize Hamzah. He said: That remains among them to this day: they weep for none but begin with Hamzah."
"12129","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Kisai narrated, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer and removed his sandals, so we removed our sandals. When he finished the prayer he said: Why did you remove your sandals? They said: We saw you remove yours, so we removed ours. He said: I got them wet."
"12130","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to address them on journeys leaning on his bow."
"12131","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir narrated, Abu Shaybah Ibrahim ibn Uthman narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to address them on journeys leaning on his bow."
"12132","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir narrated, Abu Shaybah Ibrahim ibn Uthman narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite the Opening of the Book over the funeral."
"12133","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that Ali ibn Abi Talib was the bearer of the banner of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Badr, and the bearer of the Emigrants' banner was Ali, in all the stands, and Qays ibn Sad ibn Ubadah was the bearer of Ali's banner."
"12134","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, Abu Shaybah Ibrahim ibn Uthman narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray twenty rakahs in Ramadan, and the witr."
"12135","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the disbelievers was: Come to a word equal between us and you, to the end of the verse."
"12136","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, Ibn al-Jad narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: When Abu Sufyan and his companions came down upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Uhud, he said to his Companions: I saw in a dream my sword Dhu al-Faqar broken, I saw cattle slaughtered, a calamity, and I saw my armor upon me, it is your city; they will not reach it, if Allah wills."
"12137","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Badr were one hundred water-carrying camels, two horses ridden by al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad on one while the other rested with Musab ibn Umayr, and Sahl ibn Hunayf said: his Companions took turns on the water camels on the road; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Marthad ibn Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi, ally of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, took turns on a water camel."
"12138","Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Al-Uzza was at Batn Nakhlah, al-Lat was at Taif, and Manat was at Qudayd. He said: Ali ibn al-Jad said: Batn Nakhlah is the orchard of Banu Amir."
"12139","Al-Fadl ibn Harun, companion of Abu Thawr, narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: When Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib was killed he had a striped cloak; Ali was the one who put him in his grave. When he covered his head his feet showed, and when he covered his feet his head showed, so he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and he ordered him to cover his head and take some of this idhkhir grass for his feet."
"12140","Al-Fadl ibn Harun narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Hanzalah ibn al-Rahib and Hamzah being washed by the angels."
"12141","Al-Fadl ibn Harun narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Khalid ibn al-Walid and Ali ibn Abi Talib to Yemen, appointing Ali over the Emigrants and Khalid over the Bedouins, saying: If there is fighting, Ali is over the whole people."
"12142","Al-Fadl ibn Harun narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stone the jamarat when the sun declined, so that when he finished stoning he prayed Zuhr."
"12143","Al-Fadl ibn Harun narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the stoning of Maiz ibn Malik, they came and told him they had done it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has repented a repentance that, had a tax-collector repented it, would have been accepted from him."
"12144","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jabbarah ibn Mughallis narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw Jafar ibn Abi Talib in Paradise with two wings, flying wherever he wished."
"12145","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated, Ismail ibn Aban narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah's anger is severe upon one who claims he is the king of kings."
"12146","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, author of the campaigns, narrated, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Uthman, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Eighteen hundred of Juhaynah witnessed the Conquest, a thousand of Muzaynah, nine hundred of Banu Sulaym, over four hundred of Banu Ghifar, and over four hundred of Aslam."
"12147","Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, my father narrated, Abd al-Salam ibn Rashid Abu al-Hasan al-Raffa narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that Khadijah bore the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) six: Abdullah, al-Qasim, Ruqayyah, Umm Kulthum, Fatimah, and Mariyah the Copt bore him Ibrahim."
"12148","Abu Hanifah Muhammad ibn Hanifah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hamzah ibn Jafar al-Shirazi narrated, Abu Samurah, judge of Hawar, narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of the Ansar, who is your chief? They said: Jadd ibn Qays, though we honor him. He said: He is not your chief; rather your chief is Amr ibn al-Jamuh. And he was generous."
"12149","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Awn ibn Sallam narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stone the jamarat at the sun's decline, so that when he finished stoning he prayed Zuhr."
"12150","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, Abu Shaybah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came down at Taif he ordered a caller who called: Whichever slave comes out is free. Two slaves came out to him, and he freed them."
"12151","Al-Abbas ibn al-Rabi ibn Thalab narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Ismail al-Muaddib narrated, from Fitr ibn Khalifah, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of merchants, is one of you unable, when he returns from his market, to recite ten verses, so Allah writes for him a good deed for each verse?"
"12152","Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari the judge and Muhammad ibn Shuayb al-Asbahani narrated to us, both said: Ahmad ibn Abi Surayj al-Razi narrated, Amr ibn Jumay narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us not to stone the jamarat until the sun rises."
"12153","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, al-Masudi narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ahead his weak household from Muzdalifah, then said: Do not stone the jamrah until the sun rises."
"12154","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbawayh narrated, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated, Kharijah ibn Musab narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe sweat from his face in prayer."
"12155","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Tahir ibn Abi Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated, my father narrated, Ismail ibn Abi Ishaq narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Abdullah ibn Masud came upon Abu Jahl on the Day of Badr while he was grievously wounded; he drew his sword, struck his neck and his head flew off, then took his spoils, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him he had killed Abu Jahl. He made him swear by Allah three times; he swore, and he gave him his spoils."
"12156","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth with tranquility upon him, then mentioned the hadith."
"12157","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated, from his father, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Zuhr and Asr at Mina on the Day of Tarwiyah."
"12158","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated, Shadhan narrated, Abu Kudaynah narrated, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed five prayers at Mina."
"12159","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Isa ibn Muhammad al-Simsar al-Wasiti narrated to us, both said: Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated, Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Bakr with Baraah, then followed him with Ali, who took it. Abu Bakr said: Has something happened concerning me? He said: No; you are my companion in the cave and at the Basin, and none delivers on my behalf but I or Ali."
"12160","Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Bakr ordering him to call out these words, then followed him with Ali. While Abu Bakr was on the road he heard the braying of the camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Abu Bakr came out alarmed, thinking it was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but it was Ali. He handed him the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he put him in charge of the season, and ordered Ali to call out these words. They set out and performed Hajj. Ali stood in the days of Tashriq calling: The protection of Allah and His Messenger is free of every polytheist, no naked one shall circumambulate the House, and none shall enter Paradise but a believer. Ali kept calling it, and when hoarse, Abu Hurayrah stood and called it."
"12161","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated, Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mulai, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that a man had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to give half a dinar in charity."
"12162","Yusuf the judge narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), about one who comes to his wife while she is menstruating: He gives a dinar or half a dinar in charity."
"12163","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said al-Kindi narrated, Ibrahim ibn Yazid ibn Mardanbah narrated, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), likewise."
"12164","Abu Awanah Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated, my father narrated, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated, from Matar al-Warraq, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about one who falls upon his wife while she is menstruating: He gives a dinar or half a dinar in charity."
"12165","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Awn al-Kharraz narrated, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated, Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated, al-Hakam ibn Utaybah and Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah narrated to me, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about a man who covered his wife while she was menstruating: He gives a dinar or half a dinar in charity."
"12166","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed, Muhammad ibn Rashid and Ibn Jurayj informed, both said: Abd al-Karim informed, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to his wife in her menses, let him give a dinar in charity; whoever comes to her after the blood has ceased but before she bathes, half a dinar. All that from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12167","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, Abu Jafar al-Razi informed me, from Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), about a man who had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating, he said: If it was fresh red blood, let him give a dinar in charity; if yellowish, half a dinar."
"12168","Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wakii narrated to us, my father narrated, Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated, Huraym ibn Sufyan narrated, from Layth, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying while donkeys wrestled before him."
"12169","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting and in ihram."
"12170","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated, from Sharik, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting."
"12171","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram and fasting."
"12172","Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married while in ihram and was cupped while fasting."
"12173","Muhammad ibn Khulayd al-Abdi al-Kufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated, my father narrated, from al-Hasan ibn Salih, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram."
"12174","Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Ayyub al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated, Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated, from Mamar, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, in marfu form, he said: When supper is present and prayer is established, begin with supper."
"12175","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Dawlabi narrated, Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated (ha), and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated, Salih ibn Umar narrated, both from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Al-Sab ibn Jaththamah gifted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a wild ass; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return it, for we are in ihram."
"12176","Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated, Abdullah ibn al-Ajlah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No woman admits anyone to her husband's house except with his permission, nor rises from his bed to pray except with his permission."
"12177","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated, from Salih ibn Umar, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in a red Najrani cloak he used to wear, and a shirt."
"12178","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three garments: in the shirt in which he died, and an Anbijani cloak."
"12179","Muhammad ibn Abdus narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated, Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated, from Zaidah, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in a cloak he used to wear and a shirt; al-Fadl and a man of the Ansar washed him, the Ansari pouring water over them, washing beneath the garment; he was washed with his shirt on, not removed till he was washed."
"12180","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Tarif narrated, Imran ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed effeminate men and masculinized women."
"12181","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive those who shave (their heads). A man said: And those who cut short. He said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. A man said: And those who cut short. Then on the third or fourth time he said: And those who cut short."
"12182","Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Shanaba al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, in marfu' form, he said: Charity never decreased any wealth at all, and no servant extends his hand with charity except it is placed in the Hand of Allah before it falls into the hand of the beggar, and no servant opens a door of begging when he has sufficiency without it except Allah opens for him a door of poverty."
"12183","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Uthman al-Jazari, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The first one to accept Islam was Ali."
"12184","And with the same chain likewise, from Ibn Abbas: Hamza was killed on the day of Uhud, and with him a man from the Ansar was killed, then Safiyya bint Abd al-Muttalib came with two garments to shroud Hamza in them, but there was no shroud for the Ansari man, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots between the two garments, then shrouded each one of them in a garment."
"12185","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Uthman al-Jazari, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House (the Ka'ba) and supplicated in its corners, then came out and prayed two rak'as."
"12186","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: And Uthman al-Jazari informed me, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ransomed the captives of Badr, and the ransom of each one of them was four thousand, and he killed Uqba ibn Abi Mu'ayt before the ransom; Ali ibn Abi Talib stood up to him and killed him while bound captive. He (Uqba) said: Who will look after the children, O Muhammad? He said: The Fire."
"12187","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Uthman al-Jazari, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: And when those who disbelieved plotted against you to restrain you: he said: Quraysh conferred one night at Mecca; some of them said: Restrain him with bonds, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and some of them said: Kill him, and some of them said: Expel him. So Allah informed His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of that. Ali slept on the bed of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that night, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left until he reached the cave. The polytheists spent the night guarding Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, thinking he was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When morning came they rushed upon him, and when they saw Ali, Allah turned back their plot. They said: Where is your companion? He said: I do not know. So they followed his tracks, and when they reached the mountain it became confused for them; they climbed the mountain and passed by the cave, and on its entrance was a spider's web. He remained in it three days."
"12188","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Ubayda ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Mu'adh al-San'ani narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Uthman al-Jazari, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Urwa ibn Mas'ud to al-Ta'if, then a man shot him with an arrow and killed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How much this one resembles the companion of Ya-Sin."
"12189","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ibn Shihab, Kurayb narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man would come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from among those who had set out, mentioning nothing but Hajj, and he would say: It is not Hajj, but it is Umra."
"12190","Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Bakr ibn Sulaym al-Sawwaf narrated to us, Humayd al-Kharrat narrated to us, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There are no forty (people) who intercede for a believer except Allah accepts their intercession for him."
"12191","Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani and Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Bakr ibn Sulaym al-Sufi narrated to us, Humayd al-Kharrat narrated to us, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us this supplication as he used to teach us a sura of the Qur'an: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Hell, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the False Messiah, the Dajjal, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of life and death, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the grave."
"12192","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Kurayb, from his father, from his grandfather Kurayb, that Ibn Abbas said to him: O boy, beware of reviling the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for it is distressing (grievous)."
"12193","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Kurayb, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for the weakness of the weak and the sickness of the sick, I would have delayed the night (Isha, al-Atama) prayer."
"12194","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, they said: Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Kurayb, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one consulted is trusted."
"12195","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Yahya ibn al-Ala, from Rushdayn ibn Kurayb, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man and his mother came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he intended jihad and his mother prevented him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stay with your mother, for you have with her a reward like what you have in jihad. And another came and said: I vowed to slaughter myself. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became occupied, then the man and his mother left, and he was found wanting to slaughter himself. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Praise be to Allah who placed in my umma one who fulfills the vow and fears a day whose evil is widespread. Do you have wealth? He said: Yes. He said: Sacrifice a hundred camels and make them (payable) over three years, for you will not find anyone who takes them from you all at once. Then a woman came to him and said: I am the messenger of the women to you, and there is no woman among them, whether she knew or did not know, except she desires my coming to you. Allah is the Lord of men and women and their God, and you are the Messenger of Allah to men and women. Jihad was prescribed upon men; if they gain spoils they become rich, and if they are martyred they are alive with their Lord. What of their deeds equals that? He said: Obedience to their husbands and recognition of their rights, and few among you do that."
"12196","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Rushdayn ibn Kurayb, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he drank, would breathe twice."
"12197","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Rushdayn ibn Kurayb narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I stood at his side on his left, so he took me and placed me on his right."
"12198","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to me, Abu Isma'il al-Mu'addib narrated to us, from Rushdayn ibn Kurayb, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no commander appointed over ten except he will be questioned about them on the Day of Resurrection."
"12199","Abdullah ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to me, Abu Isma'il al-Mu'addib narrated to us, from Rushdayn ibn Kurayb, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at the watering place (siqaya); a woman came with a son of hers and said: My son wants to go on campaign and I prevent him. He said: Do not leave your mother until she permits you or death takes her, for it is greater for your reward."
"12200","Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, Rushdayn ibn Kurayb narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prayer is not performed toward a grave nor upon a grave."
"12201","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, and from Thawr ibn Zayd, and from Musa ibn Maysara, from Bukayr ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever vows a vow without naming it, its expiation is the expiation of an oath; whoever vows a vow in disobedience to Allah, its expiation is the expiation of an oath; whoever vows a vow he cannot bear, its expiation is the expiation of an oath; and whoever vows a vow he can bear, let him fulfill it."
"12202","Yahya ibn Mansur Abu Sa'd al-Harawi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Bukayr ibn Abdillah narrated to him, from Kurayb, that Ibn Abbas, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Azhar, and al-Miswar ibn Makhrama said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after the Asr prayer."
"12203","Ahmad ibn Rushdayn al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to me, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bukayr ibn Abdillah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered the House, found in it an image of Ibrahim and Maryam, and said: As for them, they knew that the angels do not enter a house in which there is an image. This is Ibrahim depicted, so why is he casting lots with divining arrows?"
"12204","Ahmad ibn Rushdayn narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bukayr ibn Abdillah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he stood and performed ablution, then prayed two rak'as until that reached ten rak'as, then prayed Witr three rak'as, then lay down and slept until he snored, and his sleep was snoring, then the mu'adhdhin called him for the dawn prayer, so he went out and prayed without performing ablution."
"12205","Ahmad ibn Rushdayn narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bukayr ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after Asr."
"12206","Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj, that Kurayb, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, narrated to him, that Ibn Abbas saw Abdullah ibn al-Harith praying with his head tied up (his hair gathered) behind him; he stood behind him and began to undo it, and the other remained still for him. When he finished, he came to Ibn Abbas and said: What is it with you and my head? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The example of this is like the one who prays while bound (with hands tied)."
"12207","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir informed us, Ibrahim ibn Uqba informed me, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a gold ring on a man's hand, so he removed it and threw it away and said: One of you resorts to a coal of fire and puts it on his hand. After the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had gone, it was said to the man: Take your ring and benefit from it. He said: No, by Allah, I will not take it when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has thrown it away."
"12208","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Uqba, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A woman lifted a boy up to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Does this one have Hajj? He said: Yes, and you have reward."
"12209","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Abi Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn Uqba narrated to us, from his father, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was traveling on the road to Mecca, a woman spoke to him from her litter, and she took the arm of a boy and raised him, saying: Does this one have Hajj, O Messenger of Allah? He said: He has Hajj, and you have reward."
"12210","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Uqba, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sisters are believers: Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith, and Salma the wife of Hamza, and Asma bint Umays who is their sister through their mother."
"12211","Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Uqba, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The chief women of the people of Paradise after Maryam bint Imran are Fatima, and Khadija, and Asiya the wife of Pharaoh."
"12212","Ibrahim ibn Na'ila al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, Kurayb informed me, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Bakr in charge of the Hajj, and he did not approach the Ka'ba, but he hastened to Dhu al-Majaz informing the people of their rites and conveying to them from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until they came to Arafa before Dhu al-Majaz, and that was because they had not performed Umra along with Hajj."
"12213","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn Uqba narrated to me, from his uncle Musa ibn Uqba, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a gap between the two front teeth; when he spoke, something like light was seen between his front teeth."
"12214","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that a woman lifted up a boy of hers and said: O Messenger of Allah, does this one have Hajj? He said: Yes, and you have reward."
"12215","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us (h), and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, Muhammad ibn Uqba narrated to me, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that a woman lifted up a boy of hers and said: O Messenger of Allah, does this one have Hajj? He said: Yes, and you have reward."
"12216","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, Sharik ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Namir informed me, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I slept in the house of my maternal aunt Maymuna, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with her, to see how the night prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) talked with his family for a while then slept. When it was the last third of the night or half of it, he stood, looked at the sky and recited: Indeed in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of night and day are signs for people of understanding, until he recited these verses. Then he stood, performed ablution and cleaned his teeth, then prayed eleven rak'as. Then Bilal called the adhan for prayer, so he prayed two rak'as then went out and led the people in the dawn prayer."
"12217","Al-Hasan ibn Alawiyya al-Qattan narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Isa al-Attar narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Bishr Abu Hudhayfa narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Frequented House in heaven is called al-Surah, and it is like the Sacred House facing it; if it fell it would fall upon it. Each day seventy thousand angels enter it who never saw it at all, and it has in heaven a sanctity equal to the sanctity of Mecca. He said: And each day seventy thousand angels enter the House who never enter it again."
"12218","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Janaza ibn Salm narrated to us, from Ubaydillah ibn Umar, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Revelation came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was forty years old, then he remained after that in Mecca thirteen years, then migrated to Medina and was in it ten (years). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died when he was sixty-three years old."
"12219","Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Anbasa ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Ibn Shihab, that Kurayb narrated to him, from Ibn Abbas, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the people to dissolve (their Hajj) into Umra in the Farewell Hajj, a man would come and say: O Messenger of Allah, it is not a Hajj, it is only an Umra."
"12220","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us (h), and Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us (h), and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Masruq, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Rashdin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night with my maternal aunt Maymuna bint al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I saw him stand in the night, relieve himself, then come to the waterskin and loosen its tie, perform ablution between the two ablutions, then return to his bed and sleep, then come to the waterskin, loosen its tie and perform ablution which is the (full) ablution, then pray. I stood and did as he did, then came to him and stood on his left; he turned me and placed me on his right. He prayed either eleven rak'as or thirteen rak'as, then slept until he snored, and I heard him say in his prostration: O Allah, place in my heart light, and place in my hearing light, and place in my sight light, and place behind me light, and place before me light, and place on my right light, and place on my left light, and place above me light, and place beneath me light, and magnify for me light. Then he slept until he snored, then Bilal came to him and informed him of the prayer, so he went out."
"12221","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night with my maternal aunt Maymuna bint al-Harith. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in the night, relieved himself, then came and washed his face and hands, then stood praying the night prayer. He came to the waterskin and performed ablution between two ablutions, not excessive yet thorough. Then he stood praying. He said: And I stepped over, disliking that he see that I was watching him overnight, meaning observing him. Then I stood and did as he did, and stood on his left; he took hold of what is next to my ear until he turned me so I was on his right while he was praying. His prayer was completed to thirteen rak'as, including the two rak'as of Fajr. Then he lay down and slept until he snored, then Bilal came and informed him of the prayer, so he stood and prayed without performing ablution."
"12222","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla (h), and Isa ibn Muhammad al-Simsar al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night with my maternal aunt Maymuna bint al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: I shall observe how the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is. He came from the mosque, went to a side of the house and relieved himself, then came to the waterskin, loosened its tie and washed his face and hands. Then he took his resting place and remained as long as Allah willed. Then he stood, went to a side of the house, then came to the waterskin and loosened its tie, then performed ablution between the two ablutions, not pouring much water yet completing the ablution. Then he came to the mosque. He said: So I did as he did, then came and stood on his left; he took my hand, extended it behind him and placed me on his right. He prayed eight rak'as and prayed Witr with three, then prayed two rak'as, then said: O Allah, place for me light in my heart, and light in my hearing, and light in my sight, and light in my hair, and light in my skin, and light in my flesh, and light in my blood, and light before me, and light behind me, and light on my right, and light on my left, and light beneath me, and light above me. O Allah, give me light, and place for me light, and magnify for me light."
"12223","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'ba, Salama ibn Kuhayl narrated to me, Bukayr al-Ta'i narrated to me, from Kurayb - then I met Kurayb and he narrated to me - from Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night with my maternal aunt Maymuna and I watched how much the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prays. He stood, urinated, then came to the waterskin, loosened its tie and poured into a bowl or basin, washed his face and forearms, then slept. Then he stood and performed a good ablution between the two ablutions, and stood praying. I came and stood on his left; he took me and placed me on his right. The night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was completed as thirteen rak'as. Then he slept, and his sleep was known by his snoring; he slept until he snored, then went out to prayer. And he used to say in his prayer - or in his supplication: O Allah, place in my hearing light, and in my sight light, and in my heart light, and on my right light, and on my left light, and before me light, and behind me light, and above me light, and beneath me light, and place for me light."
"12224","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq (h), and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, both from Malik ibn Anas, from Makhrama ibn Sulayman, from Kurayb, that Ibn Abbas informed him that he spent the night with his maternal aunt Maymuna. He said: I lay across the pillow while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his family lay along it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept until midnight, or a little before or after it, then woke, sat and wiped sleep from his face with his hands, then recited the ten concluding verses of the sura of Al Imran. Then he stood to a hanging waterskin, performed ablution from it and perfected his ablution, then stood praying. I did as he did, then went and stood at his side; he placed his hand on my head and took my ear twisting it. He prayed two rak'as, then two rak'as, then two rak'as, then two rak'as, then prayed Witr and lay down until the mu'adhdhin came to him. He stood, prayed two light rak'as, then prayed the dawn prayer."
"12225","Ahmad ibn Rushdayn narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Sa'id, from Makhrama ibn Sulayman, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night with Maymuna while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with her that night. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and stood praying; I stood on his left, so he took me and placed me on his right. That night he prayed thirteen rak'as. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept until he snored, and when he slept he snored. Then the mu'adhdhin came to him, so he went out and prayed without performing ablution."
"12226","Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Iyad ibn Abdillah al-Fihri narrated to me, from Makhrama ibn Sulayman, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: My father sent me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a gift. I came to him while he was in the house of Maymuna, and he laid me down on the extra part of a pillow, until when it was midnight he stood, looked at the sky, then recited the end of the sura of Al Imran: Indeed in the creation of the heavens and the earth, until he completed it. Then he went to a hanging skin of water, cleaned his teeth, performed ablution completing it without pouring more than a little water. Then he moved me, so I stood and performed ablution. I stood on his left, so he moved me and I stood on his right. He began reciting while twisting my ear, and prayed ten rak'as, then prayed Witr, then slept, and when he slept he snored. Then Bilal came to him and woke him for prayer; he stood and bowed two light rak'as, then went out to prayer."
"12227","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Hammam informed us (h), and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one who, if he intends to come to his wife and says: In the name of Allah, O Allah, keep Satan away from us and keep Satan away from what You grant us, then a child is granted or decreed between them, whom Satan will not harm."
"12228","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i al-Qadi narrated to us, Kamil ibn Talha al-Jahdari narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Bukayr ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that he saw Abdullah ibn al-Harith praying with his head tied up behind him, so he began to undo it. When he finished he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The example of one who prays with his head tied up is like the one who prays while bound."
"12229","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to me, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that he saw Abdullah ibn al-Harith praying with his head tied up behind him; he stood behind him and began to undo it, and the other remained still for him until he finished. He said: What is it with you and my head? Ibn Abbas said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The example of one who prays with his head tied up is only like the one who prays while bound."
"12230","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a informed us, from Bukayr ibn Abdillah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House and found in it an image of Ibrahim and an image of Maryam, and said: As for them, they heard that the angels do not enter a house in which there is an image. This is Ibrahim depicted, so why is he casting lots with divining arrows?"
"12231","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Sa'd and Ibn Jurayj, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Abi Ma'bad, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All of Muzdalifa is a standing place, but keep away from the valley of Muhassir, and upon you is (to use stones) like the pebbles of khadhf (thrown between fingers)."
"12232","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abi Ma'bad, from Ibn Abbas, he said: We only knew the end of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by his takbir."
"12233","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abi Ma'bad, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, I was enlisted in such-and-such campaign while my wife is performing Hajj. He said: Return and perform Hajj with your wife."
"12234","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abi Ma'bad, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man is alone with a woman, nor travels with her, except while both are with a mahram. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I want (to join) such-and-such army while my wife is performing Hajj. He said: Then perform Hajj with your wife."
"12235","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abi Ma'bad the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman does not travel except with a mahram, and no man enters upon her except while she has a mahram with her. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to go out in such-and-such army while my wife wants Hajj. He said: Go out with her."
"12236","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abi Ma'bad the freedman of Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preached: A woman does not travel except with a mahram. A man stood and said: I was enlisted for the campaign and I intended to take my wife for Hajj. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform Hajj with your wife."
"12237","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abi Ma'bad, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No man is alone with a woman except with her is a mahram, and she does not travel except with a woman, and no man enters upon her except with a mahram. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, my wife went out performing Hajj while I was enlisted in such-and-such campaign. He said: Then turn back and perform Hajj with your wife."
"12238","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Zam'a ibn Salih narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Kurayb, or from Abi Ma'bad, that Ibn Abbas prayed in Basra upon a mat, then said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed upon a mat."
"12239","Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Umayya ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Isma'il ibn Umayya, from Yahya ibn Abdillah ibn Sayfi, from Abi Ma'bad, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sent Mu'adh to Yemen, said: You are coming to a people of Scripture, so let the first thing you call them to be the worship of Allah. When they recognize that, inform them that Allah, mighty and majestic, imposed upon them five prayers in their day and night. When they do that, inform them that Allah imposed upon them zakat taken from their wealth and returned to their poor. When they do that, take from them and beware the precious ones of their wealth."
"12240","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayya, from Yahya ibn Abdillah ibn Sayfi, from Abi Ma'bad, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like thereof."
"12241","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Awsaja the freedman of Ibn Abbas informed him, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a man died and left no one to inherit him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek. They found no one to inherit him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave his inheritance to a freedman of his whom the deceased had freed; he is the one who has the wala, he is the one who freed."
"12242","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyayna, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Awsaja the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man died in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and left no heir except a slave of his whom he had freed, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him his inheritance."
"12243","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr, from Awsaja, from Ibn Abbas, that a man died in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and no heir was found to inherit him, while he had a freedman whom the deceased had freed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give him his wealth."
"12244","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Abu Ma'bad the freedman of Ibn Abbas informed him, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The people raising the voice with dhikr upon finishing the prescribed prayer - did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do it? Ibn Abbas said: I used to know of it when I heard it."
"12245","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Abbas al-Bahili narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Awsaja, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what prevents the Habash of Banu al-Mughira from coming to you except that they fear you will turn them back. He said: There is no good in the Habash; when they hunger they steal, and when they are satiated they commit adultery, and in them are two good traits: feeding food, and strength at the time of fighting."
"12246","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Khalifa ibn Khayyat narrated to us, Hubab ibn Abdillah al-Darimi narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Hunayn the freedman of Ibn Abbas narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I spent the night with my maternal aunt Maymuna; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept then woke, performed ablution and cleaned his teeth; he did that in the night repeatedly."
"12247","Abdan narrated to us, Khalifa narrated to us, Hubab narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Hunayn narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The siwak purifies the mouth and pleases the Lord."
"12248","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Shu'ba the freedman of Ibn Abbas, he said: I witnessed Ibn Abbas when a man asked him about recitation in Zuhr and Asr. Ibn Abbas said: In them is recitation. The man said: Is it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? If the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it, I recited; and if the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not recite, I did not recite. Then the man left, so he said to me: O Shu'ba, bring him back. I brought him back, and he said: Woe to you, had he recited, the people would have known that."
"12249","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Shu'ba the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I and al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas passed on a donkey before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, and he neither forbade us nor turned us back."
"12250","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Shu'ba the freedman of Ibn Abbas, he said: al-Miswar ibn Makhrama entered upon Ibn Abbas while he wore a garment of istabraq (thick silk). He said: What is this, O Abu Abbas? He said: And what is it? He said: This istabraq. He said: I did not know of it, and I do not think the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it when he forbade it except for arrogance and pride, and we, praise be to Allah, are not like that. He said: What are these birds in the brazier? He said: Do you not see how we burned them with fire? When al-Miswar left he said: Remove this garment from me, and cut off the heads of these statues, or images."
"12251","Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Amiri al-Kufi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Shu'ba the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The whiteness of the armpits of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be seen when he prostrated."
"12252","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Shu'ba the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him with his family to Mina on the day of sacrifice, and they stoned the jamra at dawn."
"12253","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, Salama ibn Raja narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Shu'ba the freedman of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that when he washed from janaba he would pour with his right hand upon his left seven times, then said: How many times did I pour upon my hands, O Shu'ba? I said: I do not know. He said: May you have no mother, what prevents you from knowing? Then he performed ablution for prayer, then poured water over himself, then said: Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to purify himself."
"12254","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Isma'il ibn Raja, from Umayr the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Seven were forbidden through lineage, and seven through marriage. Then he recited: Forbidden to you are your mothers, until he reached: and daughters of the sister. Then he said: This is lineage. Then he recited: And your mothers who suckled you, until he reached: and that you gather together two sisters. Then he recited: And do not marry what your fathers married among women. He said: This is marriage (affinity)."
"12255","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Umayr the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from Ta'if he alighted at al-Ji'rana and distributed the spoils there, then performed Umra from it, and that was with two nights remaining of Shawwal."
"12256","Abu Amir al-Nahwi Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Suri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Tha'laba ibn Muslim informed me, from Abi Ka'b the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That Jibril, peace be upon him, was delayed from him; that was mentioned to him, and he said: How (can it be otherwise) when you do not use the siwak, nor trim your nails, nor shorten your mustaches, nor clean your finger joints."
"12257","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abida ibn Humayd narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Tamim ibn Salama, from Masruq, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and camped for rest, and nothing woke him but the sun. He stood, commanded the mu'adhdhin, who called the adhan and the iqama, then he prayed."
"12258","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban narrated to us, Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abi Wa'il, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade domestic donkeys fearing scarcity of mounts."
"12259","Abu Habib Zayd ibn al-Muhtadi al-Marwudhi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ya'qub al-Talqani narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abi al-Duha Muslim ibn Subayh, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing Allah, most high, created is the Pen and the Fish. He said: What shall I write? He said: Everything that will be until the Day of Resurrection. Then he recited: Nun, by the Pen. So al-Nun is the Fish, and al-Qalam is the Pen. None raised it from Hammad ibn Zayd except Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il."
"12260","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfa narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from his father, from Abi al-Duha, from Ibn Abbas, he said: al-Abbas came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: You left among us rancor since you did what you did. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They will not attain good until they love you, and for my kinship. Does Salhab hope for my intercession - a clan of Murad - while the sons of Abd al-Muttalib do not hope for it."
"12261","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to me, Marwan ibn Mu'awiya al-Fazari narrated to us, Abu Ya'fur Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Abu al-Duha narrated to us, Ibn Abbas narrated to us, he said: One morning the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were weeping, with each one of them her family. I went out to the mosque and it was filled with people. Umar came and ascended to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in an upper room; he greeted and he did not answer him. He said: Have you divorced your wives? He said: No, but I took an oath (of seclusion). He remained until twenty-nine (days), then came down to his family."
"12262","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began the talbiya after the prayer."
"12263","Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Mu'allal ibn Nufayl al-Harrani narrated to us, Harun ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Security and well-being - many people are cheated regarding them."
"12264","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Khusayf, from Ikrima and Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade pure silk; as for its warp or weft being silk, there is no harm in wearing it. And he forbade the silver vessel."
"12265","Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani and Ja'far al-Qalanisi narrated to us, they said: Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: I ask you no reward for it except that you honor me for myself due to my kinship to you, and preserve the kinship between me and you."
"12266","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Khusayf, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated, he turned the inside of his palms toward his face."
"12267","Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Missisi narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd al-Fara'idi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Harun ibn Hayyan, from Khusayf, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None shall enter Paradise who has a mustard seed's weight of arrogance."
"12268","Al-Husayn ibn Ja'far al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn al-Khalil al-Khazzaz narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not pass the appointed time (miqat) without ihram."
"12269","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us, from Attab ibn Bashir, from Khusayf, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: We knew that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the footgear and his Companions wiped; so did he wipe after the sura of al-Ma'ida was revealed?"
"12270","Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi and Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Awaqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Abi al-Waddah narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: Say, I ask you no reward for it except love for kinship. He said: There was no clan among the clans of Quraysh except he was born of them or had kinship among them. Say, I ask you no reward for it except that you protect me and refrain from me due to my kinship to you."
"12271","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to me, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that a man was thrown by his camel and died while in ihram. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not bring perfume near him; for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiya."
"12272","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Farrukh narrated to me, Abu Farwa narrated to me, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, raising it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever prays four rak'as after the last Isha, reciting in the first two rak'as: Say, O disbelievers, and: Say, He is Allah, One, and reciting in the last two rak'as the revelation of al-Sajda, and: Blessed is He in whose Hand is dominion, they are written for him like four rak'as of Laylat al-Qadr."
"12273","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Marwan ibn Shuja' narrated to us, he said: I only remember Salim al-Aftas narrating to me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Healing is in three: a drink of honey, the incision of a cupper, and cauterization with fire; and I forbid my umma from cauterization."
"12274","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ubayd ibn Nistas al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world. He said: The questioning in the grave: Who is your Lord? What is your religion? Who is your Prophet? And in the Hereafter likewise."
"12275","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Tuhawi narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Qur'an came down all at once, then it came down upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in portions."
"12276","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Ubayda ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to me (h). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abdillah ibn Zurara al-Raqqi narrated to us, they said: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Rabah ibn Ma'ruf al-Makki narrated to us, from Salim ibn Ajlan al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that Abdullah ibn Abdillah ibn Ubayy - his father said to him: O my son, seek for me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a garment of his garments to shroud me in, and order him to pray over me. Abdullah said: O Messenger of Allah, you know the nobility of Abdullah, and he ordered me to seek from you a garment to shroud him in, and that you pray over him. He gave him a garment of his garments and intended to pray over him. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, you know Abdullah and his hypocrisy; will you pray over him when Allah forbade you to pray over him? He said: And where? He said: If you ask forgiveness for them seventy times, Allah will never forgive them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall increase upon it. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: And never pray over any of them who dies, nor stand over his grave. And Allah revealed: It is the same for them whether you ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them; Allah will never forgive them. He said: And a man entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and prolonged sitting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out three times so he would follow him, but he did not. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, entered, saw the man and recognized dislike on the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) due to his sitting. He said: Perhaps you harmed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The man understood and stood. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I stood three times for you to follow me, but you did not. He said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you took a chamberlain, for your wives are not like other women, and it is purity for their hearts. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet except when permitted to you, to the end of the verse. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Umar and informed him of that. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consulted Abu Bakr and Umar regarding the captives. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, be considerate to your people and take ransom from them and seek help with it. Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Kill them. He said: If you two agreed, I would not disobey you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the view of Abu Bakr. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: It is not for a prophet to have captives until he has made slaughter in the land; you desire the goods of this world while Allah desires the Hereafter. He said: Then there came down: And We created man from an extract of clay, to the end of the verses. Umar said: Blessed be Allah, the best of creators. Then there was revealed: So blessed be Allah, the best of creators."
"12277","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Talha al-Yarbu'i narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Sharik, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, the polytheists mocked him and said: Muhammad mentions the god of Yamama, while Musaylima used to call himself al-Rahman. When this verse came down, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded not to recite it aloud."
"12278","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Muti' al-Ghazzal, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to him and said: I made my wife forbidden upon me. He said: She is not forbidden upon you. Then he recited: O Prophet, why do you forbid what Allah made lawful for you. But upon you is the severest of expiations, a slave."
"12279","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that an animal be tied up (as a target to shoot at)."
"12280","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, I think from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a man enters Paradise he asks about his parents, wife and children. It is said: They did not reach your rank and deed. He says: O Lord, I worked for myself and for them. So they are commanded to be joined with him. And Ibn Abbas recited: And those who believed and their offspring followed them in faith, to the end of the verse."
"12281","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mu'awiya al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: Ta-Ha. He said: O man."
"12282","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Mu'alla ibn Mansur al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The daughter of Khalid ibn Sinan came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he spread his garment for her and said: The daughter of a prophet whom his people neglected."
"12283","Ahmad ibn al-Ja'd al-Washsha narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Atiyya narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not pray before the two Eids nor after them."
"12284","Ahmad ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Atiyya narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Hajj is jihad, and Umra is voluntary."
"12285","Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Isma'il al-Qattan al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us, Isa ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank standing."
"12286","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us (h). And Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jandal ibn Waliq narrated to us, they said: Ubaydillah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be in the last times a people who dye with black like the crops of birds; they will not smell the fragrance of Paradise."
"12287","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us (h), and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi' al-Burani narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: While Jibril, peace be upon him, was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he heard a creaking sound from above him, so he raised his head and said: This is a gate of heaven opened today which was never opened except today. An angel descended from it and said: This is an angel who descended to earth and never descended except today. He greeted and said: Rejoice in two lights given to you which no prophet before you was given: the Opening of the Book, and the concluding verses of the sura of al-Baqara; you do not recite a letter of them except you are given it."
"12288","Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Tamim narrated to me, from Ali ibn Badhima, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I approached my wife while she was menstruating. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to free a slave, and the value of a slave that day was a dinar."
"12289","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us (h), and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dispense with people even with a fragment of siwak."
"12290","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Ahwal narrated to us, Abu Ubayda ibn Ma'n narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A barren wind seized them on the day of Badr."
"12291","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Harb ibn al-Hasan al-Tahhan narrated to us, Husayn al-Ashqar narrated to us, from Qays, from al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When there was revealed: Say, I ask you no reward for it except love for kinship. They said: O Messenger of Allah, who are these kin of yours whose love became obligatory upon us? He said: Ali and Fatima and their two sons, may Allah be pleased with them."
"12292","Abdullah ibn al-Abbas al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When there was revealed: Those whom the angels take in death while wronging themselves, to the end of the verse, he said: There were a people in Mecca who had accepted Islam; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) migrated to Medina they disliked migrating and feared. Then Allah, most high, revealed: Those whom the Angels take in death, to His saying: Except the weak."
"12293","Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn Ubaydillah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: When it was Thursday - and what is Thursday - then he wept and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me a sheet and inkwell; I shall write for you a writing after which you will never go astray. They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is delirious. Then they fell silent and he fell silent. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not bring you afterward? He said: Afterward."
"12294","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade taking anything possessing a soul as a target."
"12295","Ibrahim ibn Na'ila al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Abu Maryam narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take anything possessing a soul as a target."
"12296","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb and Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us (h), and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, they said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on the day of Fitr, and did not pray before it nor after it. Then he came to the women while Bilal was with him and ordered them to give charity. The woman began to cast her earring and necklace."
"12297","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Shu'ba, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, raising it, he said: Whoever hears the call then does not come to it, there is no prayer for him except with an excuse."
"12298","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Ma'mar al-Qati'i narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Abi Janab al-Kalbi, from Maghra, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever hears the call and does not answer without an excuse, there is no prayer for him."
"12299","Ibrahim ibn Na'ila al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Abu Maryam narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When al-Aqra' ibn Habis addressed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) interjected in the midst of his speech and said: Indeed some eloquence is magic."
"12300","Ibrahim ibn Abdillah ibn Ayyub al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us, Abu Tumayla narrated to us, from Abi Hamza, from Jabir, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: Indeed He who imposed the Qur'an upon you will return you to the place of return. He said: Death, or to Mecca."
"12301","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yazdad al-Kufi narrated to us, Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take anything possessing a soul as a target."
"12302","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abdillah al-Bakka'i narrated to us, Umar ibn Abdillah ibn Ya'la al-Thaqafi narrated to us, al-Minhal ibn Amr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expiated with a sa' of dates, and ordered the people to do so; whoever does not find, then with half a sa'."
"12303","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Aqal al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abi Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge for Hasan and Husayn: I seek refuge for you two with the perfect words of Allah from every devil and venomous creature and from every envious eye."
"12304","Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Humayd, the son-in-law of Abdullah ibn Musa, narrated to us, al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from Shu'ba, from Maysara ibn Habib, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever visits a sick person whose appointed time has not come, and says with him seven times: I ask Allah the Mighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you, except he is cured."
"12305","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Sayfi ibn Rib'i narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he called for me a pillow of coarse haircloth and placed it under my head."
"12306","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Hakkam ibn Salm narrated to us, from Anbasa, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Muhammad asked his Lord not to clothe them in factions, nor make them taste each other's violence, but He refused."
"12307","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Arhabi narrated to us, from Ubayda ibn al-Aswad, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whose prayer Allah does not accept: an imam of a people while they dislike him, and a woman who spends the night while her husband is angry with her, and two brothers who have cut each other off."
"12308","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not show mercy to our young, honor our elder, and recognize our right."
"12309","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Mu'afa al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no man who visits a sick person and says: I ask Allah the Mighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you, seven times, while there is delay in his appointed time, except it is lightened for him."
"12310","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I read to al-Fudayl ibn Maysara, from Abi Hariz, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no deed more beloved to Allah than a deed in these ten days, except a man who goes out striving with himself and his wealth, then does not return."
"12311","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us (h). And Abu Ma'n Thabit ibn Nu'aym al-Hawji narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us (h). And Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Sa'ib informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night in which I was taken by night journey, I found a pleasant scent. I said: What is this pleasant scent, O Jibril? He said: This is the scent of the hairdresser of Pharaoh's daughter and her children. I said: What is her story? He said: While she was combing Pharaoh's daughter, the comb fell from her hand, so she said: In the name of Allah. Pharaoh's daughter said: My father? She said: No, but my Lord and your Lord and the Lord of your father is Allah. She said: And you have a lord other than my father? She said: Yes. She said: Shall I inform him of that? She said: Yes. She informed him, so he called her and said: O so-and-so, do you have a lord other than me? She said: Yes, my Lord and your Lord is Allah. He ordered a cow of copper which was heated, then her children were taken and cast into it one by one. She said: I have a need of you. He said: And what is it? She said: I would like my bones and the bones of my child gathered in one cloth and you bury us together. He said: That is yours upon us. Her children kept being cast into the cow until it reached a nursing son of hers; she seemed to hesitate for his sake. He said to her: O mother, plunge in, for the punishment of this world is easier than the punishment of the Hereafter. Ibn Abbas said: Four young ones spoke: Isa ibn Maryam, and the companion of Jurayj, and the witness of Yusuf, and the son of the hairdresser of Pharaoh. And the wording is that of the hadith of Abu Umar al-Darir."
"12312","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salama, with its chain, the like thereof."
"12313","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfa Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Sulayman the Prophet of Allah, peace be upon him, when he stood in his place of prayer would see a tree standing before him. He would say to it: What is your name? It would say: The carob. He would say: For what are you? It would say: For the ruin of this House. Sulayman said: O Allah, conceal my death from the jinn until men know that the jinn do not know the unseen. He said: He carved it into a staff to lean upon; the termite ate it and it fell, so he fell down. They estimated the termite's eating and found it a year. So men realized that had the jinn known the unseen, they would not have remained a year in the humiliating punishment. And Ibn Abbas used to recite it thus. The jinn thanked the termite, so they would bring it water wherever it was."
"12314","Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasa'i narrated to us, Amr ibn Yazid Abu Burayd al-Jarmi informed us, Sayf ibn Ubaydillah narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prostration is upon seven limbs: the hands, the feet, the knees, and the forehead; and raising the hands when you see the House, and upon al-Safa and al-Marwa, and at Arafa and at Muzdalifa, and at stoning the jamras, and when the prayer is established."
"12315","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Hashim al-Tusi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy prophets prayed in the mosque of al-Khayf, among them Musa, as if I see him wearing two Qatawani cloaks, in ihram upon a camel of the camels of Shanu'a, bridled with a bridle of fiber, having two braids."
"12316","Ja'far ibn Ahmad al-Sami al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sabbah al-Muzani narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you sneezes and says: Praise be to Allah, the angels say: Lord of the worlds. When he says: Lord of the worlds, the angels say: May Allah have mercy on you."
"12317","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Black Stone was whiter than snow until the sins of the children of Adam blackened it."
"12318","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Sa'd ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, my grandfather Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated to me, my father narrated to me, Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was commanded with the siwak until I feared for my teeth."
"12319","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Raqashi narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the footgear, then said: Ask these who claim that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the footgear after the sura of al-Ma'ida; by Allah, he did not wipe after al-Ma'ida. For me to wipe upon the back of a mule is more beloved to me than to wipe upon them."
"12320","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I never saw people better than the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they asked him only about thirteen questions until he died, all of them in the Qur'an, among them: They ask you about the sacred month, and: They ask you about wine and gambling, and they ask you about orphans, and: And they ask you about menstruation, and: They ask you about the spoils, and: They ask you what they spend. They only asked about what benefits them. He said: And the first to circumambulate the House were the angels, and between the Stone and the Yemeni Corner are graves of the graves of the prophets. And when his people harmed the Prophet, he would go out from among them and worship Allah in them until he died."
"12321","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib - Hammad ibn Zayd said, I think, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr - from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (h). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I asked my Lord a request and I wished I had not asked Him. I said: O Lord, there were messengers before me; among them those for whom You subjected the winds, and among them those who gave life to the dead. He said: Did I not find you an orphan and shelter you? Did I not find you astray and guide you? Did I not find you poor and enrich you? Did I not expand for you your breast and remove from you your burden? He said: I said: Yes indeed, O Lord. And their wording is one."
"12322","Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisa ibn Uqba narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bowl of tharid and said: Eat from its sides, and do not eat from its middle, for blessing descends in its middle."
"12323","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Abu Hamza narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to show him the rites; Thabir split open for him, so he entered Mina and showed him the jamras, then showed him Muzdalifa and showed him Arafat. When he was at the jamra, Iblis appeared to him, so he stoned him with seven pebbles and he sank away. Then he appeared to him until he mentioned the jamra of Aqaba, and he sank away and went."
"12324","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that Jibril, peace be upon him, went with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the jamra of Aqaba; Satan confronted him, so he stoned him with seven pebbles and he sank away. Then he came to the farthest jamra; Satan confronted him, so he stoned him with seven pebbles. When Ibrahim, peace be upon him, intended to slaughter Ishaq, he said to his father: When you slaughter me, withdraw lest I writhe and my blood spill upon you. So he bound him. When he took the knife and intended to slaughter him, he was called from behind him: O Ibrahim, you have fulfilled the vision."
"12325","Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Safwan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Jibril went with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to show him the rites; he brought him to the jamra of Aqaba, and Iblis was upon it. He commanded him and he stoned him with seven pebbles, and he sank into the earth. Then he came to the middle jamra, and he was likewise; then he recited the talbiya from Arafat."
"12326","12294 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated, Imran ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Fitr, and he began with the prayer before the sermon, with neither adhan nor iqamah. Then he mounted his riding animal and delivered the sermon upon it. Then he came to the women and addressed them and urged them to give charity, saying: Give charity, O company of women. So a woman would cast off her garment and her ring and her earring, and all of that was gathered to Bilal in his garment."
"12327","12295 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban reported to me, Imran ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Jews disputed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Do you eat from what we kill, but you do not eat from what Allah kills? So Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: {And do not eat of that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned}."
"12328","12296 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated, from Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, regarding: {And whether you reveal what is in yourselves or conceal it, Allah will hold you to account for it}: He said: When it was sent down, that weighed heavily upon the Muslims and distressed them, so Allah abrogated it, and Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: {Allah does not burden a soul except with what it can bear}."
"12329","12297 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Musa ibn Abi A'ishah, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Qur'an would descend upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would receive it with his tongue and his lips, and he would endure great strain from that. So Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: {Do not move your tongue with it to hasten it} — meaning: to hasten taking it — {Indeed, it is upon Us to gather it and recite it} — meaning: to gather it, that We gather it in your breast and that you recite it — {So when We recite it} — i.e., when We send it down — {then follow its recitation} — meaning: listen and be silent — {Then it is upon Us to make it clear} — that We make it clear with your tongue. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found rest."
"12330","12298 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Musa ibn Abi A'ishah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the saying of Allah, mighty and majestic: {Woe to you, and woe} {Then woe to you, and woe}: Is it something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, or something Allah sent down? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it, then Allah sent it down."
"12331","12299 - Ubayd ibn Kathir al-Tammar narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Furat al-Qazzaz narrated, (H). And Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Musarrif ibn Amr al-Yami narrated — both saying: al-Harith ibn Imran al-Ja'fari narrated, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: While I was circumambulating with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he heard a man saying: O Allah, forgive so-and-so, the son of so-and-so. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this? He said: A man ordered me to supplicate for him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your companion has been forgiven."
"12332","12300 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated, Sufyan narrated, he said: Mis'ar ibn Kidam said, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We wished that Musa had remained patient with him, so that he would have related to us more of the story of the two of them."
"12333","12301 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married while he was in ihram."
"12334","12302 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The dreams of the Prophets are revelation."
"12335","12303 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Isra'il narrated, from Simak, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: {You are the best nation brought forth for mankind}: He said: They are those who emigrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Madinah."
"12336","12304 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, (H). And Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq — both of them, from Isra'il, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Ma'iz came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and confessed twice, then he said: Take him away. Then he said: Bring him back, and he confessed twice, until he had confessed four times. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take him away and stone him."
"12337","12305 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ma'iz ibn Malik: Is what has reached me about you true? He said: And what has reached you about me? He said: It has reached me that you fell upon the slave girl of the sons of so-and-so. He said: Yes. Then he bore witness four testimonies, and he ordered that he be stoned, and he was stoned."
"12338","12306 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar reported to me, al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ma'iz: Is what has reached me about you true? And he mentioned the like of the hadith of Abu Awanah."
"12339","12307 - Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi and Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuza'i al-Isbahani narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Isra'il narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the shade of a room upon which the shade had almost shrunk away, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man will come to you who will look at you with the two eyes of a devil, so when he comes to you, do not speak to him. They had not waited long before a man appeared before them. He called him and said: For what do you revile me, you and your companions? He said: Call them. So they called them, and they began to swear by Allah that they had neither said nor done anything, until he pardoned them. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: {On the day Allah resurrects them all, they will swear to Him as they swear to you} — the verse."
"12340","12308 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"12341","12309 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Simak, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"12342","12310 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Isra'il narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The dwellings of the Ansar were far from the mosque, and they wanted to move closer to the mosque, so there was sent down: {And We record what they send forth and their traces}. So they remained firm in their dwellings."
"12343","12311 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sahl ibn Salih al-Antaki narrated, Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Sabiq narrated, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would supplicate in qunut in Fajr against a clan of Banu Sulaym."
"12344","12312 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, (H). And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated — both saying: Sufyan narrated, from al-Mughirah ibn al-Nu'man, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, naked and uncircumcised. Then he recited: {As We began the first creation, We shall repeat it — a promise upon Us; indeed, We shall do it}. The first to be clothed will be Ibrahim, and men from my companions will be seized to the right and to the left. I shall say: My companions! It will be said: They kept turning back upon their heels ever since you parted from them. So I shall say as the righteous servant Isa, the son of Maryam, said: {And I was a witness over them as long as I remained among them; when You took me, You were the Watcher over them, and You are Witness over all things * If You punish them, they are Your servants; and if You forgive them, indeed You are the Mighty, the Wise}."
"12345","12313 - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Missisi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Mughirah ibn al-Nu'man, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Marry, for the best of this nation were those with the most wives."
"12346","12314 - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-Mughirah ibn al-Nu'man, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, regarding: {And whoever kills a believer intentionally}: He said: There is no repentance for the killer of a believer; no verse has abrogated it since it was sent down."
"12347","12315 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Hakam narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from al-Mughirah ibn al-Nu'man, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: The people of Kufah differed over it, so I went to Ibn Abbas, and he said: It was sent down among the last of what was sent down, and nothing has abrogated it."
"12348","12316 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated, Hibban ibn Ali narrated, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: Is there anyone from Hudhayl among you? No one answered him. Then he said: Is there anyone from Hudhayl among you? A man said: I am, though a man from among them has died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What prevented you from speaking when I spoke? He said: I thought, O Messenger of Allah, that something had been sent down concerning my people, and I disliked being the one to bring it to them. He said: No; your companion is held back because of his debt."
"12349","12317 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated, Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am ruined! He said: And what has ruined you? He said: I turned my saddle over. He did not answer him anything until there was sent down: {Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish} — meaning: from the front and from behind — and avoid blood and menstruation."
"12350","12318 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Umar ibn al-Abbas al-Razi narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated, Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah, Iblis let out a wail, and his troops gathered to him. He said: Despair of ever turning the nation of Muhammad to shirk after this day of yours, but tempt them in their religion and spread wailing among them."
"12351","12319 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated, Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while he was fasting and in ihram."
"12352","12320 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini narrated, from Ya'qub al-Qummi, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would never leave fasting the white days, neither on a journey nor at home."
"12353","12321 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Harithi narrated, Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a man from the Ansar. When he drew near his house he heard him speaking inside. When he sought permission and entered, he saw no one. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I heard you speaking to someone other than yourself. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I had entered inside, grieved by the talk of the people because of the fever in me, and there entered upon me one entering — I have never seen any man after you with a nobler gathering or finer speech than him. He said: That was Jibril, peace be upon him. And indeed, among you are men such that if one of them were to swear by Allah, He would fulfill it."
"12354","12322 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Quraysh came to the Jews and said: With what did Musa come to you? They said: His staff, and his hand white to the beholders. And they came to the Christians and said: How was Isa? They said: He would heal the blind and the leper and give life to the dead. Then they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Supplicate your Lord for us to make al-Safa gold for us. So he supplicated his Lord, and this verse was sent down: {Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of night and day are signs for those of understanding} — so let them reflect upon it."
"12355","12323 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both saying: Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray two rak'ahs after Maghrib, lengthening the recitation in them until the people of the mosque would disperse."
"12356","12324 - Abu Husayn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Quraysh would circumambulate the House while naked, whistling and clapping. So Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: {Say: Who has forbidden the adornment of Allah}. Then they were commanded to wear garments."
"12357","12325 - al-Fadl ibn Abi Rawh al-Basri narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated, from Ash'ath ibn Ishaq, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding: {Indeed, the allies of Allah — there is no fear upon them, nor do they grieve}: He said: Allah is remembered upon seeing them."
"12358","12326 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no days in which deeds are more beloved to Allah, mighty and majestic — or he said: more excellent in them — than the ten days. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, not even jihad? He said: Not even jihad, except a man who goes out with himself and his wealth and returns with nothing of that."
"12359","12327 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shu'bah informed, from al-A'mash, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No deed in any days is more excellent than in the ten of Dhul Hijjah. They said: O Messenger of Allah, not even jihad in the path of Allah? He said: Not even jihad in the path of Allah, unless a man goes out with himself and his wealth, then returns with nothing of that."
"12360","12328 - Musa ibn Zakariyya al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Habib ibn Abi Amrah, and al-A'mash, and Mukhawwal, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There are no days of the world in which deeds are more excellent than the ten days. A man said: Not even the like of them in the path of Allah? Three times. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the third: Unless he does not return."
"12361","12329 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shu'bah informed, from al-A'mash, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned to him that her sister had vowed to fast a month, and that she had boarded the sea, then died without fasting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast on behalf of your sister."
"12362","12330 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated, Za'idah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has died and a month's fast is due upon her; shall I make it up on her behalf? He said: If your mother had a debt, would you settle it on her behalf? He said: Yes. He said: Then the debt of Allah is more deserving of being settled. Sulayman said: So al-Hakam and Salamah ibn Kuhayl said, while we were all sitting when Muslim narrated this hadith: We heard Mujahid mention this hadith from Ibn Abbas."
"12363","12331 - Ahmad ibn Isma'il al-Razi narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Bakr al-Razi narrated, my father reported to me, from al-Jarrah ibn al-Dahhak, from al-A'mash, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother imposed upon herself the fast of a month, but she has died. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tell me, if she had a debt, would you settle it? He said: Yes. He said: Then the debt of Allah is more deserving of being settled."
"12364","12332 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: My father reported to me, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated, from al-A'mash, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father has died and he did not perform Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: If your father had a debt, would you settle it? He said: Yes. He said: Then the debt of Allah is more deserving of being settled."
"12365","12333 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father reported to me, Waki' narrated, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite on Friday in the Fajr prayer {Alif Lam Mim, the revelation} — al-Sajdah — and {Has there come upon man}."
"12366","12334 - al-Hasan ibn Ulayl narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Waki' narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite on Friday in the Fajr prayer {Alif Lam Mim, the revelation} — al-Sajdah — and {Has there come upon man}, and he would recite in Jumu'ah {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} and {Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming}."
"12367","12335 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated, Waki' narrated, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he recited {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}, would say: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High."
"12368","12336 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from al-A'mash, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Makkah, Abu Bakr said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has been expelled — we shall all perish. Then when this verse was sent down: {Permission has been given to those who are fought, because they were wronged; and indeed Allah is able to grant them victory * Those who were expelled from their homes}, Abu Bakr knew that there would be fighting."
"12369","12337 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, (H). And Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqal al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated — both saying: Ghannam ibn Ali narrated, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray two rak'ahs in the night, then leave and use the siwak."
"12370","12338 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Rabi'ah Fahd ibn Awf narrated, (H). And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Talib narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Be brief in prayer, for behind you are the weak, the elderly, and the one with a need."
"12371","12339 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated, Jarir narrated, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit and Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man who believes in Allah and the Last Day hates the Ansar, and no man who believes in Allah and the Last Day loves Thaqif."
"12372","12340 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Abu al-Muhayyah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed five prayers at Mina."
"12373","12341 - Ali ibn al-Abbas al-Bajali al-Kufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Tasnim narrated, Hasan ibn Husayn al-Arabi narrated, Yahya ibn Isa al-Ramli narrated, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umm Salamah: This is Ali ibn Abi Talib; his flesh is my flesh and his blood is my blood. He is to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."
"12374","12342 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was at Qudayd, the rump of a donkey, and he returned it dripping with blood."
"12375","12343 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father reported to me, Ibn Abi Layla narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the rump of a donkey dripping with blood, and he returned it, saying: We are in ihram."
"12376","12344 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever hears the call and does not answer it, then there is no prayer for him. Thus al-Qatrani narrated it from Sulayman ibn Harb as mawquf, and Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated it from Sulayman ibn Harb as marfu'."
"12377","12345 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi and Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad narrated to us, both saying: Asim ibn Ali narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The first to be called to Paradise are the much-praising, those who praise Allah in ease and hardship."
"12378","12346 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, said: Son of Adam, as long as you call upon Me and hope in Me, I shall forgive you for whatever is in you. Even if you were to come to Me with sins filling the earth, I would meet you with forgiveness filling the earth, as long as you do not associate anything with Me. And even if your sins reached the clouds of the sky, then you sought My forgiveness, I would forgive you."
"12379","12347 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Assal al-Isbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated, Abu Maryam narrated, Habib ibn Abi Thabit reported to me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Ka'bah and prayed two rak'ahs between the two pillars. Then he came out and prayed two rak'ahs between the door of the House and the Stone. Then he said: This is the qiblah. Then he entered another time and stood supplicating, and did not pray."
"12380","12348 - Mahmud ibn al-Faraj al-Isbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated, Hammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The people of shirk would chant the talbiyah: Labbayk, O Allah, labbayk; labbayk, You have no partner except a partner who belongs to You — You own him and what he owns. So Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: {Do you have, among what your right hands possess, any partners in what We have provided you, so that you are equal therein, fearing them as you fear one another}."
"12381","12349 - Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated, Kamil Abu al-Ala narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night at my aunt Maymunah's. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose, startled, and fetched water and performed ablution. Then he recited {Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth} to the end of the surah. Then he began al-Baqarah and recited it letter by letter until he completed it. Then he bowed and said: Glory be to my Lord, the Tremendous. Then he prostrated and said: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High. Then he raised his head and said between the two prostrations: My Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, mend me, raise me, provide for me, and guide me. Then he stood and recited in the second rak'ah Al Imran until he completed it. Then he bowed and prostrated, then did as he had done in the first. Then he reclined, then rose, startled, and did the like of what he had done in the first two, reciting letter by letter, until he had prayed eight rak'ahs, reclining between every two rak'ahs, and he prayed witr with three. Then he prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr. Then he said: O Allah, place light in my self, and light in my heart, and light in my sight, and light in my hearing, and place light before me, and light behind me, and light on my right, and light on my left, and light beneath me, and light above me, and magnify light for me."
"12382","12350 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated, Abu Maryam narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed sa'y between al-Safa and al-Marwah."
"12383","12351 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued chanting the talbiyah until he stoned the jamrah."
"12384","12352 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When there was sent down {And warn your nearest kin}, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended al-Safa and said: O cry of the morning!"
"12385","12353 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Allah took the covenant of the Prophets upon their peoples."
"12386","12354 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said, regarding {And they withhold al-ma'un}: It is lending."
"12387","12355 - al-Husayn ibn Ja'far al-Qattat narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, (H). And Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, (H). And Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid informed — all of them, from al-Shaybani, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-dubba, al-hantam and al-naqir, and mixing dates and raisins."
"12388","12356 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi and Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, both saying: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated, al-Mas'udi informed, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I vowed to slaughter at Buwanah. He said: Perhaps there is something of the affair of Jahiliyyah in your heart? He said: No. He said: Then fulfill your vow."
"12389","12357 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Musafir narrated, Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated, al-Mas'udi narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The last verse sent down is: {And fear a day in which you will be returned to Allah}."
"12390","12358 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus al-Ramli narrated, Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated, from al-Mas'udi, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, regarding: {And We did not send you except as a mercy to the worlds}: He said: Whoever follows him, it is a mercy for him in this world and the Hereafter; and whoever does not follow him is spared what the rest of the nations were afflicted with of metamorphosis, sinking and pelting."
"12391","12359 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated, my father narrated, from Husayn ibn Dhakwan, from Amr ibn Khalid, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade walking in a single sandal or a single khuff, spending the night alone in a house, relieving oneself in an open expanse of land without bending down, or meeting an enemy without warding him off from oneself."
"12392","12360 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus al-Ramli narrated, Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated, from al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Abu Isra'il while he was standing in the sun, and said: What is the matter with this one? They said: O Messenger of Allah, he vowed not to speak, not to sit, and to fast. He said: Order him to speak, to seek shade, to sit, and to complete his fast — and he did not order him to make expiation."
"12393","12361 - Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated, Abd Allah ibn Bazigh narrated, al-Hasan ibn Umarah narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that a man fell from his riding animal and died, so they asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Wash him with lote leaves and water, shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his head, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection chanting the talbiyah."
"12394","12362 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived, and the Jews were fasting the day of Ashura. He said: What is the matter with this day? He said: It is a day in which Allah saved Musa and drowned the Children of Isra'il, so we have more right to Musa. So he fasted it and ordered fasting it."
"12395","12363 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Salamah ibn Shabib narrated, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated, Kamil Abu al-Ala narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say between the two prostrations: My Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, grant me health, and provide for me."
"12396","12364 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shabib al-Isbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated, Abu Maryam narrated, al-Hakam narrated, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother vowed to fast a month, but she died before she fasted. He said: Tell me, if your mother had a debt, would you settle it? She said: Yes. He said: The debt of Allah is more deserving of being settled."
"12397","12365 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, (H). And Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated — both saying: Shu'bah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night at my aunt Maymunah's. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, then came and prayed four rak'ahs, then slept. Then he rose and said: Has the boy woken — has the little boy stood? I came, and I stood on his left, and he moved me to his right. Then he prayed five rak'ahs, then prayed two rak'ahs, then slept until I heard his snoring — or he said: his breathing. Then he went out to prayer."
"12398","12366 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, (H). And Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated — both saying: Shu'bah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was at Qudayd, the thigh of a donkey — or he said: the rump of a wild donkey — and he returned it dripping with blood, while he was in ihram."
"12399","12367 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated, he said: I heard Mansur reporting from al-Hakam, (H). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Jarir narrated, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah gifted the leg of a wild donkey dripping with blood to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was in ihram at Qudayd, and he returned it dripping with blood."
"12400","12368 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated, my father narrated, from Abu Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam and Sa'id ibn Jubayr: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of al-Khandaq: They have distracted us from the middle prayer; may Allah fill their graves and their bellies with fire."
"12401","12369 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Hasan ibn Furat al-Qazzaz narrated, Ali ibn Hashim narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Minhal ibn Amr and al-Hakam, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I owe the freeing of a slave, and I have a black, non-Arab slave girl. He said: Bring her to me. Then he said: Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah? She said: Yes. He said: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? She said: Yes. He said: Free her."
"12402","12370 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abbad ibn Ziyad narrated, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from al-Hakam, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that a black slave came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: A wayfarer passes by me while I am among my master's livestock, so may I give him to drink from their milk without their permission? He said: No. He said: Then I shoot, hitting dead-on and wounding. He said: Eat what you strike dead-on, and leave what you merely wound."
"12403","12371 - Bishr ibn Musa and Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, both saying: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, my father narrated, from Isma'il ibn Sumay', from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shows off, Allah will expose him; and whoever seeks repute, Allah will make him notorious."
"12404","12372 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated, Sharik narrated, from Mukhawwal, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray witr with three, reciting in the first {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}, in the second {Say: O disbelievers}, and in the third {Say: He is Allah, the One}."
"12405","12373 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, (H). And Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated, Za'idah narrated, from Sufyan, from Mukhawwal, from Muslim al-Batin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in Jumu'ah the surah al-Jumu'ah and the surah al-Munafiqun."
"12406","12374 - Uthman ibn Amr al-Dabbi and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, both saying: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shu'bah informed, from Mukhawwal, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in Jumu'ah the surah al-Jumu'ah and the surah al-Munafiqun."
"12407","12375 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, both saying: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shu'bah informed, from Mukhawwal, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in the morning prayer on Friday {Alif Lam Mim, the revelation} and {Has there come upon man}."
"12408","12376 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Mukhawwal ibn Rashid, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday {Alif Lam Mim, the revelation} — al-Sajdah — and {Has there come upon man}."
"12409","12377 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya narrated, Sharik narrated, from Mukhawwal, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"12410","12377 / 2 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Amrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Muslims loved that the Romans should prevail over the Persians, because they were People of the Book; and the idolaters loved that the Persians should prevail over the Romans, because they were people of idols. The Muslims mentioned that to Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Indeed, they shall be defeated. Abu Bakr mentioned that to them, and they said: Set a term between us and you of five years. But they did not prevail. Abu Bakr mentioned that to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he said: Why did you not set it — I think he said — less than ten? He said: Sa'id said: Al-bid' is less than ten. He said: Then the Romans prevailed afterwards. That is His saying: {Alif Lam Mim * The Romans have been defeated * In the nearest land, and they, after their defeat, shall overcome * Within a few years}. He said: The Romans were defeated, then the Romans overcame afterwards. He said: {To Allah belongs the command before and after, and on that day the believers shall rejoice * With the help of Allah}."
"12411","12378 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani and al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us, both saying: al-Fayd ibn Wathiq al-Thaqafi narrated, Jarir narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Amrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed the Jews; fats were prohibited to them, so they sold them and consumed their prices."
"12412","12379 - Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Jarud al-Isbahani narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Zibyan al-Mazini narrated, Ja'far ibn Salamah al-Warraq narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Ali ibn Ata ibn Muqaddam narrated, Habib ibn Abi Amrah narrated, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment in which was al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad. When they came to the people, they found them dispersed, and there remained a man with much wealth who had not left. He said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. Al-Miqdad lunged at him and killed him. A man from his companions said to him: You killed a man who said: There is no god but Allah; by Allah, that shall surely be mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they said: O Messenger of Allah, a man bore witness that there is no god but Allah, yet al-Miqdad killed him. He said: Call al-Miqdad to me. Then he said: O Miqdad, you killed a man who said: There is no god but Allah; how will you do with: There is no god but Allah? He said: Then Allah sent down: {O you who believe, when you go forth in the path of Allah, verify, and do not say to one who offers you peace: You are not a believer — seeking the fleeting goods of the life of this world; with Allah are many spoils. Thus you were before, then Allah favored you}. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He was a believing man hiding his faith among a disbelieving people, and you killed him; and likewise you used to hide your faith in Makkah."
"12413","12380 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from Abd al-Majid ibn Suhayl, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr: that Ibn Abbas reported to him that his father, Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, sent him on an errand of his to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Maymunah bint al-Harith was the maternal aunt of Ibn Abbas. He entered upon her and found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque. Ibn Abbas said: So I reclined in her room, intending in myself to count how much the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed. He said: He came while I was reclining in the room after part of the night had passed, and said: Has the boy slept? Then he took a mantle that was upon Maymunah, wrapped himself in part of it while part of it remained upon her. Then he stood and prayed two by two until he had prayed eight rak'ahs. Then he prayed witr with five, without sitting between them. Then he sat and praised Allah with what He deserves, praising abundantly. Then the last of his speech was: O Allah, make for me light in my heart, and make for me light in my hearing, and make for me light in my sight, and make for me light on my right, and light on my left, and make for me light before me, and light behind me, and increase me in light, and increase me in light, and increase me in light."
"12414","12381 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from al-A'mash, from Hassan Abi al-Ashras, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Qur'an was separated from the Remembrance and placed in the House of Might in the lowest heaven. Then Jibril would bring it down upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), reciting it distinctly."
"12415","12382 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jumhur ibn Mansur narrated, Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar narrated, al-A'mash narrated, Hassan Abu al-Ashras narrated, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: {Indeed, We sent it down in the Night of Decree}: He said: The Qur'an was sent down all at once until it was placed in the House of Might in the lowest heaven, and Jibril, peace be upon him, brought it down upon Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in response to the speech of the servants and their deeds."
"12416","12383 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi al-Hakam al-Thaqafi narrated, Asim ibn Mudarris al-Nasri narrated, from Jabalah ibn Sulayman, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first adhan was only instituted so that the people of prayer may prepare for their prayer. When you hear the adhan, perfect the ablution; and when you hear the iqamah, hasten to the first takbirah, for it is the branch of prayer and its completion. And do not hasten the reciter to bow and prostrate."
"12417","12384 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated, Husayn al-Ashqar narrated, Nusayr ibn Ziyad narrated, from Uthman Abi al-Yaqzan, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Ansar said among themselves: If we were to gather wealth for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so that he extends his hand with no one coming between him and it. They came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we wish to gather for you from our wealth. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: {Say: I do not ask you for any reward except love for kin}. They left differing: some of them said: Did you not see what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said? And some of them said: He only said this so that we fight for his household and support them. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: {Or do they say: He has forged a lie against Allah} — up to His saying: {And it is He who accepts repentance from His servants}. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) presented repentance to them — up to His saying: {And those who believe and do righteous deeds respond, and He increases them of His bounty} — they are those who said this: that you repent to Allah and seek His forgiveness."
"12418","12385 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Umar ibn Dharr al-Hamadhani narrated, he said: I heard my father reporting from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Jibril, peace be upon him: What prevents you from visiting us more often than you visit us? Then this verse was sent down: {And we descend not except by the command of your Lord}."
"12419","12386 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ali ibn Qutaybah al-Rifa'i narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated, Umar ibn Dharr narrated, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding the prostration of Sad: Dawud prostrated it in repentance, and we prostrate it in gratitude."
"12420","12387 - al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Umar ibn Dharr, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it — and he did not mention Ibn Abbas."
"12421","12388 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far narrated, from Abi al-Sahba, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of my household is the likeness of the ship of Nuh; whoever boards it is saved, and whoever stays behind from it drowns."
"12422","12389 - al-Hasan ibn Sahl ibn al-Mujawwiz al-Basri narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated, Mansur ibn Dinar informed, from Hammad, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Wine was prohibited in itself, and intoxicants of every drink."
"12423","12390 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated, from al-Nu'man ibn Thabit Abi Hanifah, from Hammad, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent the weak ones of his household by night to Jam', and said to them: Do not stone the jamrah until the sun rises."
"12424","12391 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Hammad, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while he was fasting."
"12425","12392 - al-Hasan ibn Sahl ibn al-Mujawwiz al-Basri narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated, from Sufyan, from Abd al-A'la, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever speaks about the Book of Allah without knowledge, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"12426","12393 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, (H). And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated — both saying: Abu Awanah narrated, from Abd al-A'la, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"12427","12394 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jumhur ibn Mansur narrated, Sayf ibn Muhammad narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abd al-A'la, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"12428","12395 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il narrated, Isra'il narrated, from Abd al-A'la, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that a man reviled a father of al-Abbas from Jahiliyyah, so al-Abbas slapped him. His people came and said: By Allah, he shall surely be slapped, and they bore arms. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ascended the pulpit and said: O people, which people of the earth do you know to be noblest to Allah? They said: You. He said: Then al-Abbas is from me and I am from him. Do not revile our dead, lest you harm our living. Then the people came and said: O Messenger of Allah, we seek refuge in Allah from your anger; seek forgiveness for us."
"12429","12396 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn al-Isbahani narrated, Hakkam ibn Salm narrated, from Ali ibn Abd al-A'la, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lahd is for us, and the shaqq is for others."
"12430","12397 - Abd Allah ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far narrated, my father reported to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated, from Abd al-A'la, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is prohibited by suckling is what is prohibited by lineage."
"12431","12398 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, all saying: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Marry, for the best of us were those with the most wives."
"12432","12399 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Abu Shihab narrated, from al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When wine was prohibited, the companions of the Messenger of Allah walked to one another and said: Wine has been prohibited, and it has been made equal to shirk."
"12433","12400 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abi Sakhr, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, regarding {The heart did not lie about what it saw}: He said: He saw Him."
"12434","12401 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abi Sakhr, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When Allah sent down {Except the weak among men, women and children who can find no means, nor are guided to a way} — the going out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12435","12402 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Amr al-Ash'athi narrated, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated, from Humayd al-Kharrat, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: {My Lord, make this a secure land and provide its people with fruits — those of them who believe in Allah and the Last Day}: Ibn Abbas said: Ibrahim, peace be upon him, had reserved it for people to the exclusion of others, so Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: And the disbeliever too — I shall provide them as I provide the believers. Would I create a creation and not provide for them? I shall grant them enjoyment a little, then compel them to the punishment of the Fire. Then Ibn Abbas recited: {We extend to these and these from the gift of your Lord, and the gift of your Lord is not restricted}."
"12436","12403 - Muhammad ibn al-Rabi' ibn Shahin narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Jabir, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me, for Satan does not take my likeness."
"12437","12404 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated, from Sufyan, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, regarding {His Kursi extends over the heavens and the earth}: He said: The place of the two Feet, and the measure of His Throne cannot be estimated."
"12438","12405 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Farwah ibn Abi al-Maghra narrated, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Concession was granted to the very old man, the one seized by intense thirst, and the pregnant woman to break the fast in Ramadan."
"12439","12406 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Utbah ibn Humayd al-Dabbi, from Umar ibn Abd Allah al-Thaqafi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and said: Advise me. He said: I advise you to fear Allah, and beware of mentioning the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for you do not know what has preceded for them."
"12440","12407 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated, Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Utbah narrated, Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the one in ihram does not find a waist-wrapper, let him wear trousers; and whoever does not find sandals, let him wear khuffs."
"12441","12408 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father reported to me, Uthman ibn Umar narrated, Malik ibn Mighwal narrated, from al-Shaybani, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring and wore it. Then he said: This has distracted me from you since today — a glance to it and a glance to you. Then he cast it away."
"12442","12409 - al-Hasan ibn Alluwayh al-Qattan narrated to us, Abbad ibn Musa al-Khuttali narrated, Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated, from Habib ibn Hassan, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my nation shall enter Paradise without reckoning."
"12443","12410 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated, from Abi Ma'shar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would circumambulate the House wearing red mantles, and they were not of the thin kind."
"12444","12411 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Abd Allah al-Wasiti narrated, my father narrated, Umar ibn al-Khattab, a man from the people of Kufah, reported to me, from Sufyan ibn Ziyad, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My nation has been given something no one of the nations was given at the time of calamity: {Indeed, we belong to Allah and to Him we return}."
"12445","12412 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated, Umar ibn Thabit narrated, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, regarding: {I swear by this land} — Makkah — {while you are free in this land} — Makkah — {and by the father and what he begot * Certainly We created man in hardship} — in uprightness and erect posture."
"12446","12413 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Shayban Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from Ash'ath ibn al-Sha'tha, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah does not look at one who drags his garment."
"12447","12414 - Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us, both saying: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated, Sharik narrated, from Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed, Allah, mighty and majestic, does not look at one who drags his waist-wrapper."
"12448","12415 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both saying: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abd al-Rahim narrated, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A sheep passed in front of the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in prayer, between him and the qiblah, and it did not cut off his prayer."
"12449","12416 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Zakariyya al-Kufi narrated, Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated, from Muslim al-Mula'i, from Mujahid and Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing was opened upon Ad of the wind except the like of the place of a ring. Then it was sent upon them, and it carried the desert-dwellers to the settled people. When the settled people saw it, {they said: This is a cloud bringing us rain}, facing our valleys. The people of the deserts were in it, and it cast the people of the desert upon the people of the settled land until they perished. He said: It rebelled against its keepers until it came out through the gates."
"12450","12417 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, Hammam narrated, from Qatadah, from Azarah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in the morning prayer on Friday {Alif Lam Mim, the revelation} — al-Sajdah — and {Has there come upon man}."
"12451","12418 - al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated, my father narrated, Hammam narrated, from Qatadah, from Azarah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in the Jumu'ah prayer the surah al-Jumu'ah and al-Munafiqun."
"12452","12419 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Azarah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah. He said: Who is Shubrumah? He said: My brother, or a relative of mine. He said: Have you performed Hajj? He said: No. He said: Perform Hajj on your own behalf, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah."
"12453","12420 - Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad narrated, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Azarah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the nabidh of al-jarr. So I came to Ibn Abbas and mentioned that to him, and he said: Ibn Umar spoke the truth. I said: What is al-jarr? He said: Of baked clay."
"12454","12421 - Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi, the scribe of Bakkar al-Qadi, narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli narrated, Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Malik al-Sulami narrated, from Qatadah, from Azarah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What an excellent gift is a word of truth that you hear, then carry it to a Muslim brother of yours and teach it to him."
"12455","12422 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated, Hammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated, from Abi Farwah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in every Jumu'ah in the morning prayer {Alif Lam Mim, the revelation} and {Has there come upon man}."
"12456","12423 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ka'b narrated, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated, from Muslim al-Mula'i, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wiping over the khuffs is for the resident a day and a night, and for the traveler three days and their nights."
"12457","12424 - al-Husayn ibn Ja'far narrated to us, al-Min-jab ibn al-Harith narrated, Ali ibn Mushir narrated, from Muslim al-Mula'i, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was aided with al-saba, and Ad were destroyed with al-dabur."
"12458","12425 - al-Hasan ibn Ghulayb al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr on the day of Ashura, and when he finished he said: Whoever among you woke up fasting, let him complete his fast; and whoever did not wake up fasting, let him not eat anything. For this is a day in which Musa was granted victory over Pharaoh, so the Jews fasted it in gratitude, and we have more right to gratitude."
"12459","12426 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated, Sharik narrated, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, regarding {So I swear by the setting places of the stars}: He said: The Qur'an was sent down all at once to the lowest heaven, then it came down in portions afterwards to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12460","12427 - Ya'qub ibn Ghaylan al-Umani narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, from Abi Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Nusayr ibn Abi al-Ash'ath, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of your garments are white, so shroud your dead in them and clothe your living in them. And the best of your kohls is ithmid; it grows hair and clears the sight."
"12461","12428 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Isra'il narrated, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas — he raised the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever dies addicted to wine shall meet Allah like a worshiper of idols."
"12462","12429 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Abd Allah ibn al-Walid al-Ijli narrated, from Bukayr ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Jews came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Abu al-Qasim, we ask you about things; if you answer us in them, we shall follow you, believe you and have faith in you. He said: So he took upon them what Isra'il took upon himself. They said: Allah is witness over what we say. They said: Inform us about the sign of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: His two eyes sleep, but his heart does not sleep. They said: Inform us, how does the woman produce a female and how does she produce a male? He said: The two fluids meet; if the fluid of the woman overcomes the fluid of the man, she produces a female, and if the fluid of the man overcomes the fluid of the woman, she produces a male. They said: You spoke the truth. They said: Then inform us about thunder, what is it? He said: An angel among the angels entrusted with the clouds, directing them wherever Allah wills. They said: Then what is this sound that is heard? He said: The rebuke of the clouds when he rebukes them until they reach where he commanded them. They said: You spoke the truth. They said: Then inform us what Isra'il forbade upon himself? He said: He used to dwell in the desert, then he fell ill and found nothing that suited him except the meat of camels and their milk, so for that he forbade them. They said: You spoke the truth. They said: Then inform us who comes to you among the angels, for there is no prophet but an angel among the angels comes to him with the message and the revelation; so who is your companion? Only this remains. He said: Jibril, peace be upon him. They said: That is the one who descends with war and fighting; he is our enemy. Had you said Mikail, who descends with rain, we would have followed you. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, sent down: {Say: Whoever is an enemy to Jibril} — the verse."
"12463","12430 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ubayd al-Qasim ibn Sallam narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed, from Sufyan, from Abi Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade killing any creature tied up as a target."
"12464","12431 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated, Isra'il narrated, from Abi Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The jinn would ascend to the heaven, listening to the revelation. When they heard a word, they added nine to it: the word would be true, but what they added would be false. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent, they were barred from their seats. That was mentioned to Iblis — and the stars had not been pelted with before that. Iblis said to them: This is for a matter that has occurred on earth. So he sent his troops, and they found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing praying between two mountains. They came to him and informed him, and he said: This is the matter that has occurred on earth."
"12465","12432 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in reported to me, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was born in the Year of the Elephant."
"12466","12433 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin and Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Wadih al-Assal al-Misriyyan narrated to us, both saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abi Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in Jumu'ah in the morning {Alif Lam Mim, the revelation} — al-Sajdah — and {Has there come upon man}."
"12467","12434 - Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman al-Kilabi narrated, Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated, from Abi Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray witr with {Glorify}, and {Say: O disbelievers}, and {Say: He is Allah, the One} — a surah in each rak'ah."
"12468","12435 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated, Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Nabidh would be prepared for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the house of my maternal aunt, in a waterskin."
"12469","12436 - Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Banan ibn Muhammad al-Daqqaq narrated, al-Hasan ibn Atiyyah narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Abi Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no days in which a deed drawing near to Allah is more excellent than these ten days. It was said: Not even jihad? He said: Not even jihad, unless one strives with himself and his wealth and returns with nothing of it."
"12470","12437 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father reported to me, he said: I found in the book of my father, in his handwriting, from Imran ibn Abi Imran, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever follows the Book of Allah, Allah shall guide him from misguidance and protect him from an evil reckoning on the Day of Resurrection. That is because Allah says: {Then whoever follows My guidance shall neither go astray nor suffer}."
"12471","12438 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Salm ibn Abi al-Dhayyal, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no musa'ah (illicit sexual liaison) in Islam; whoever practiced musa'ah in the pre-Islamic ignorance, I have attached him to his paternal kin, and whoever claims a child not born of a lawful bed neither inherits nor is inherited from."
"12472","12439 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us, Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will be gathered barefoot, naked, uncircumcised."
"12473","12440 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: My maternal aunt Umm Hufayd gave to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clarified butter, dried cheese, and mastigures (desert lizards); he ate of the clarified butter and the dried cheese and left the mastigures out of distaste, and had it been unlawful it would not have been eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12474","12441 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us (ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us; both said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that Umm Hufayd bint al-Harith ibn Juzayy, the maternal aunt of Ibn Abbas, gave to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clarified butter, dried cheese, and mastigures; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for them and they were eaten at his table, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left them as one who finds them distasteful, and had they been unlawful they would not have been eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor would he have ordered that they be eaten."
"12475","12442 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah on the day of Ashura and found the Jews fasting, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this? They said: This is a day on which Allah drowned Pharaoh and saved Moses, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have more right to Moses (peace be upon him); then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded its fast."
"12476","12443 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, my sister vowed to perform Hajj and died without performing Hajj. He said: Tell me, if your sister had owed a debt, would you have paid it? He said: Yes. He said: Then the debt of Allah is more deserving to be paid; perform Hajj on behalf of your sister."
"12477","12444 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that a woman from Juhaynah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My mother vowed to perform Hajj and did not perform Hajj until she died; shall I perform Hajj on her behalf? He said: Tell me, if your mother had owed a debt, would you have paid it? She said: Yes. He said: Then perform Hajj on her behalf and fulfill what is due upon her, for Allah, mighty and majestic, is most deserving of fulfillment."
"12478","12445 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas regarding the saying of Allah, mighty and majestic: When the help of Allah and the victory come: he said: His own soul was announced to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); there was revealed to him: When the help of Allah and the victory come - the conquest of Makkah - so seek forgiveness from your Lord, and know that your appointed time has come."
"12479","12446 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us (ha). And Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us (ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us; they said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never fasted a complete month other than Ramadan, and when he fasted, he would fast until one would say: By Allah, he will never break his fast, and when he broke his fast, he would break it until one would say: By Allah, he will never fast."
"12480","12447 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us (ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us; both said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba (gourds), hantam (green jars), and muzaffat (pitch-coated vessels)."
"12481","12448 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us (ha). And Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us; Abu Awanah informed us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said: Allah knows best what they would have done when He created them."
"12482","12449 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us (ha). And Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us; both said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, and Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out with a group of his Companions heading toward the market of Ukaz, while the devils had been barred from the news of heaven and the shooting stars had been sent against them, so the devils returned to their people, who said: What is wrong with you? They said: We have been barred from the news of heaven, and the shooting stars have been sent against us. They said: Nothing has barred you from the news of heaven except something that has newly happened, so strike through the easts of the earth and its wests and see what it is that has barred you from the news of heaven. So they set out striking through the easts of the earth and its wests, seeking what had barred them from the news of heaven, and that band which had headed toward Tihamah turned back toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he and his Companions were at Nakhlah heading toward the market of Ukaz, and he was leading his Companions in the dawn prayer; when they heard the Qur'an they listened, and said: By Allah, this is what has barred you from the news of heaven. Thereupon, when they returned to their people, they said: O our people, Indeed, we have heard a wondrous Qur'an; it guides to righteousness, so we have believed in it, and we will never associate anyone with our Lord. Then Allah revealed to His Prophet: Say, it has been revealed to me; and what was revealed to him was only the saying of the jinn."
"12483","12450 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Hammad al-Ma'ni narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr - I know it only - from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited al-Najm, and when he reached: Have you considered al-Lat and al-Uzza, and Manat, the third, the other - Satan cast upon his tongue: those exalted gharaniq (cranes), whose intercession is hoped for. When he prostrated, the Muslims and the polytheists prostrated, so Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: And We did not send before you any messenger or prophet but that when he recited, Satan cast - up to His saying: the punishment of a barren day - the day of Badr."
"12484","12451 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Nu'aym al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seeing with one's own eyes is not like being told; Allah said to Moses: Your people have been tempted, yet he did not cast down the tablets, but when he saw with his own eyes, he cast down the tablets and broke them."
"12485","12452 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Mahan narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: When I take the two precious ones (the eyes) of My servant and he is patient and seeks reward, I am not pleased with any reward for him less than Paradise."
"12486","12453 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ja'far ibn Iyas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: They used to dislike giving from their kinship shares to their polytheist relatives, so they asked and were given permission; then this verse was revealed: It is not upon you to guide them, but Allah guides whom He wills, and whatever good you spend is for yourselves - up to His saying: and you will not be wronged."
"12487","12454 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abadah ibn Ziyad al-Asadi narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyyah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas regarding His saying: And neither recite your prayer aloud nor lower it, but seek a way between: he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them aloud with the Qur'an, the polytheists would hear it and revile him and revile the One who brought it, so Allah revealed to him: And do not recite your prayer aloud, lest the polytheists hear it and revile it; and do not lower it - he said: Let your Companions hear - but seek a way between."
"12488","12455 - Abu Shubayl Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Waqid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Nafi' al-Dabbi, from Qatadah and Ja'far ibn Iyas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas regarding the saying of Allah, mighty and majestic: And when they hear what was revealed to the Messenger, you see their eyes overflowing with tears: he said: They were sailors - meaning seamen - who came with Ja'far ibn Abi Talib from Abyssinia; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited the Qur'an, they believed and their eyes overflowed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps when you return to your land you will turn away from your religion. They said: We will never turn away from our religion; then Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed that as part of their saying."
"12489","12456 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymunah's, and it was her night; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to pray, so I stood at his left, and he took hold of my forelock, or my hair, and placed me at his right."
"12490","12457 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Mahdi al-Attar al-Kufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Bazigh narrated to us, Mus'ab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, from Abu Mu'adh, from Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyyah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim but that he has a sin which he commits time after time; the believer is forgetful, but when he is reminded, he remembers."
"12491","12458 - Ja'far ibn Ahmad al-Shami al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Subayh narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Samman narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyyah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to her: What prevents you from Hajj? She said: We had only a water-carrying camel upon which my father and my husband went out to battle. He said to her: Perform Umrah in Ramadan, for it counts for you as a Hajj."
"12492","12459 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Rabi'ah ibn Kulthum ibn Jabr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The prohibition of wine was revealed concerning two tribes of the Ansar who drank until, when they became intoxicated, some of them jested roughly with others; when they sobered up, a man would see the mark on his face, head, and beard, saying: My brother so-and-so did this to me; by Allah, had he been compassionate and merciful to me, he would not have done this to me. And they were brothers with no malice in their hearts, but malice then fell into their hearts, so Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: Wine, gambling, idols, and divining arrows are but defilement from the work of Satan, so avoid them that you may prosper; Satan only wants to cause enmity and hatred among you through wine and gambling, and to hinder you from the remembrance of Allah and from prayer; will you then desist? Then some strict people said: It is defilement, yet it is in the belly of so-and-so who was killed on the day of Badr, and so-and-so who was killed on the day of Uhud; so Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they tasted - the verse."
"12493","12460 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Farqad al-Sabakhi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that a woman brought a son of hers to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my son is possessed by madness, and it seizes him at our lunch and dinner, troubling us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped his chest and supplicated, and he vomited a vomit, and there came out of his belly something like a black puppy, and he was cured."
"12494","12461 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq who said: I heard Umar ibn Rashid narrating from Ya'la ibn Hakim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: Declaring unlawful (for oneself) is an oath. And Ibn Abbas said: You have indeed in the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) an excellent example."
"12495","12462 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Misri narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the dawn prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim, the Revelation - al-Sajdah, and: Has there come upon man."
"12496","12463 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Abu Abdullah al-Khurasani narrated to me, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: Allah obligated prayer through the tongue of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as four (units) in residence and two units on journey."
"12497","12464 - Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Waki'i narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Mu'ammil ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr who said: Ibn Abbas said: Marry, for the best of us was the one with the most wives."
"12498","12465 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Hamzah ibn al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated to us, from his father, from Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued pronouncing the talbiyah until he stoned the Aqabah pillar."
"12499","12466 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, Asim ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymunah's; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to pray at night, so I stood at his left, and he took my hand and placed me at his right, wiped my chest, and said: O Allah, grant him wisdom."
"12500","12467 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Nu'aym al-Wasiti narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abu Hashim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Shall I not inform you of your men among the people of Paradise in this world? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is in Paradise, the truthful one is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, the newborn born in Islam is in Paradise, and the man who is at the edge of town visiting his brother, visiting him only for Allah, is in Paradise. Shall I not inform you of your women among the people of Paradise? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The fertile, loving one who, when she angers or he angers, says: My hand is in your hand; I shall not sleep."
"12501","12468 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Hashim al-Rummani, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"12502","12469 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi narrated to us (ha). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us; both said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu Hashim al-Rummani, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Death has a terror, so when the death of one of your brothers comes to any of you, let him say: Indeed we belong to Allah and indeed to Him we shall return; and indeed we shall return to our Lord; O Allah, write him among the doers of good, place his record in Illiyyun, raise up his progeny among those who remain, O Allah, do not deprive us of his reward, nor tempt us after him."
"12503","12470 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Bishr al-Kahili narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Hashim al-Rummani, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: Thirty-nine men and women accepted Islam along with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Umar accepted Islam completing the forty; then Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: O Prophet, Allah is sufficient for you and those of the believers who follow you."
"12504","12471 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Jabir ibn Kurdi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from Abu Hashim al-Rummani, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymunah's; when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed Isha, he returned to her, and it was her night; he prayed two units, then turned, and said: Has the boy slept? - while I was listening - then he said in his prayer: O Allah, place light in my heart, light in my hearing, light in my sight, light in my tongue, and grant me light."
"12505","12472 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gabriel (peace be upon him) came to me and said: Convey greetings to Umar and tell him: His pleasure is judgment (wisdom), and his anger is might."
"12506","12473 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Bishr ibn Ma'mar al-Qarqasa'i narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Zayd al-Ammi narrated to us, from his father (ha). And Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Dawud al-Sukkari al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khulayd al-Hanafi narrated to us, Salm ibn Salim narrated to us, from Nuh ibn Abi Maryam, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever acts for Allah in congregation and is correct, Allah accepts it from him, and if he errs, He forgives him; and whoever acts seeking division, if he is correct, Allah does not accept it from him, and if he errs, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"12507","12474 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abu Salih Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, from Ata ibn Dinar al-Hudhali, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that he said regarding the saying of Allah, mighty and majestic: That your Lord may raise you to a praised station: he said: He seats him between Himself and Gabriel, and he intercedes for his nation; that is the praised station."
"12508","12475 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever claims affiliation to other than his father, or allies himself to other than his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"12509","12476 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married while in ihram, and was cupped while in ihram."
"12510","12477 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married while in ihram, and was cupped while in ihram."
"12511","12478 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions performed Umrah from al-Ji'ranah; they uncovered their right shoulders, placed their cloaks under their armpits and threw them over their shoulders, then walked briskly."
"12512","12479 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will surely resurrect the (Black) Stone on the Day of Resurrection with two eyes with which it sees and a tongue with which it speaks, bearing witness for whoever touched it in truth."
"12513","12480 - Al-Walid ibn al-Abbas al-Addas al-Misri narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: In a muddy spring."
"12514","12481 - Al-Hasan ibn Ghulayb al-Misri narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Ja'far al-Ramli narrated to us, Abd al-Majid ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Truffles are of the manna, and their water is a cure for the eye. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed for sciatica the fat of a ram's tail."
"12515","12482 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, saying: I found in my father's book: Abu al-Ashja' gave us his father's book, and we copied from it: from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I slaughtered before stoning. He said: Stone, and there is no harm."
"12516","12483 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"12517","12484 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, saying: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He mentioned his Lord, mighty and majestic; He said: When My servant remembers Me alone, I remember him alone, and when he remembers Me in a company, I remember him in a company better than the company in which he remembered Me."
"12518","12485 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Abdullah Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear white of your garments, for they are among the best of your clothes, and shroud your dead in them; and among the best of your kohl is ithmid (antimony), for it grows hair and clears vision."
"12519","12486 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"12520","12487 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of your garments is white, so clothe your living in it, and shroud your dead in it."
"12521","12488 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym al-Makki narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Wear white of your garments, for they are the best of your garments, and shroud your dead in them; and the best of your kohl is ithmid, for it clears vision and grows hair."
"12522","12489 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear white of your garments, for they are among the best of your garments, and shroud your dead in them; and among the best of your kohl is ithmid, for it clears vision and grows hair."
"12523","12490 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah and Abu Awanah together narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear these white garments, for they are among the best of your garments, and shroud your dead in them; and among the best of your kohl is ithmid, for it clears vision and grows hair."
"12524","12491 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Apply ithmid, for it clears vision and grows hair."
"12525","The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear white garments, and shroud your dead in them."
"12526","12492 - Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi' al-Burani narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear white of your garments, for they are among the best of your garments, and shroud your dead in them; and the best of your kohl is ithmid, for it clears vision and grows hair."
"12527","12493 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki and al-Husayn ibn Humayd al-Akki al-Misri narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated to us, Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Laythi narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the best of your garments is white, so clothe your living in it, and shroud your dead in it; and the best of your kohl is ithmid, for it clears vision and grows hair."
"12528","12494 - al-Hasan ibn Alluyah al-Qattan narrated to us, Abbad ibn Musa al-Khuttali narrated to us, Abu Isma'il al-Mu'addib narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sit on the ground, eat on the ground, hobble the sheep (with his own hand), and accept the invitation of the slave to barley bread."
"12529","12495 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sahl ibn Zanjalah al-Razi narrated to us, al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I took from a woman everything short of intercourse itself; then Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the watches of the night."
"12530","12496 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding: Alike are the dweller therein and the visitor: he said: Alike are the resident and the one who departs."
"12531","12497 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abdullah al-Bakka'i narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad, freedman of the family of Zayd ibn Thabit, narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, and Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: A Jewish man called al-Nabbash ibn Qays said: Your Lord is stingy and does not spend; so Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: And the Jews said: The hand of Allah is chained; chained are their hands, and cursed are they for what they said; rather, His two hands are outstretched; He spends as He wills."
"12532","12498 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was turned from Syria toward the qiblah, and prayed toward the Ka'bah in Rajab, seventeen months after his arrival in Madinah."
"12533","12499 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a group of merchants and said: O company of merchants. They responded to him and stretched their necks. He said: Allah will resurrect you on the Day of Resurrection as wicked evildoers, except whoever was truthful, righteous, and fulfilled trust."
"12534","12500 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Jamil al-Marwazi narrated to us (ha). And Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi narrated to us, Hibban ibn Musa and Suwayd ibn Nasr narrated to us; they said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Rabah ibn Zayd, from Umar ibn Habib, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When Allah created the Pen, He said to it: Write; so it flowed with what shall be until the establishment of the Hour."
"12535","12501 - al-Hasan ibn Alluyah al-Qattan narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Isa al-Attar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Ayyash, from Ja'far ibn al-Harith, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Jurayj, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Is there repentance for one who kills a believer intentionally? He said: No. I said: Then where is His saying: And those who do not call upon another god with Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit adultery, and whoever does that shall meet punishment; multiplied for him shall be the punishment on the Day of Resurrection, and he shall abide therein disgraced; except whoever repents and believes and does righteous work, for those Allah will change their evil deeds into good deeds? He said: This is a Meccan verse abrogated by a Medinan verse: And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell, abiding therein, and Allah is angry with him, curses him, and has prepared for him a great punishment."
"12536","12502 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us, Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water and was brought a large bucket of Zamzam; he lapped in it and drank while standing."
"12537","12503 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said - and I think it is from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that when he raised his head from bowing he would say: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever You will after that."
"12538","12504 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muslim ibn Hatim al-Ansari narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid al-Qurashi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymunah's; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose at night, performed ablution three times three times, then stood to pray; I stood and did what he did, then stood at his left, and he moved me to his right."
"12539","12505 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade musmat (a garment) of silk."
"12540","12506 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Harun ibn Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa narrated to us, my father narrated to us (ha). And Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Samarqandi narrated to us, Hashim ibn Makhlad narrated to us; both from Shibl ibn Abbad al-Makki, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that he poured ablution water for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at his maternal aunt Maymunah's; when he came out he said: Who placed my ablution water for me? She said: Your nephew, O Messenger of Allah. He said: O Allah, give him understanding in religion and teach him interpretation."
"12541","12507 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Harun ibn Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shibl ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: Thursday - and what is Thursday - a day on which the pain of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intensified; and he mentioned the hadith."
"12542","12508 - Ja'far ibn Ahmad al-Shami al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Mukhtar ibn Ghassan narrated to us, from Abu Muhayyah Yahya ibn Ya'la, from his father, from Abd al-Malik ibn Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I am holding you by your waistbands away from the Fire, saying: Beware of Hell, beware of the prescribed punishments; when I die, I shall precede you, and our appointment is at the Pond; whoever comes to it shall prosper, and some people shall come and be taken to the left; I shall say: O Lord, my nation. It shall be said: You do not know what they innovated after you, turning back upon their heels."
"12543","12509 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, saying: Salih al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim, from Abd al-Malik ibn Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: Adi ibn Badda and Tamim al-Dari used to travel to Makkah for trade; a man of Banu Sahm went out with them and died in a land where there was no Muslim; he entrusted his estate to them, and they delivered his estate to his family but kept a silver cup inlaid with gold. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made them both swear by Allah that they had neither concealed nor released these; then the cup was found in Makkah, and they said: We bought it from Tamim al-Dari and Adi. Two men among the guardians of the Sahmi stood, swore, and took the cup; and concerning them this verse was revealed: O you who believe, the testimony between you - the verse."
"12544","12510 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Malik, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Moses performed Hajj upon a red bull, wearing a Qatawani cloak."
"12545","12511 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Malik ibn Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah created a Preserved Tablet of white pearl, its pages of red ruby; its pen is light; Allah has in it every day three hundred and sixty glances: creating, providing, causing death, giving life, honoring, humbling, and doing what He wills."
"12546","12512 - Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Mahan narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us, Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: A woman from Juhaynah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother died without performing Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on her behalf? He said: Tell me, if your mother had owed a debt and you paid it, would that suffice for her? She said: Yes. He said: Then the debt of Allah is more deserving to be paid."
"12547","12513 - Ali ibn al-Abbas al-Bajali al-Kufi and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah."
"12548","12514 - al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah did not send a prophet to a people and then take him but that He made after him an interval (fatrah); then He fills Hell from that interval."
"12549","12515 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from al-Jarrah ibn al-Minhal, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr who said: I was in a circle in which was Ibn Abbas, and we mentioned divine decree; Ibn Abbas became intensely angry and said: If I knew that among the people was one of them (a denier of decree), I would seize him; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah did not send a prophet among a people and then take him but that He made after him an interval, and filled Hell from that interval."
"12550","12516 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us (ha). And Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and Asr in Madinah without travel or fear. I said to Ibn Abbas: Why do you think he did that? He said: He wanted that none of his nation be burdened."
"12551","12517 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and Asr, and combined Maghrib and Isha in Madinah while resident, without fear or anything compelling him to it. They said: Why, O Abu Abbas? He said: He wanted that his nation not be burdened."
"12552","12518 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr and Asr together in Madinah without fear or travel."
"12553","12519 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Qawwas narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha."
"12554","12520 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us (ha). And Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us; both from Qurrah ibn Khalid, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha, on a journey, or in the campaign of Tabuk."
"12555","12521 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha, while traveling."
"12556","12522 - Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Abi al-Dumayk al-Mustamli narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ziyad Sabalan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Ta'ifi, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that he said to his sons: O my sons, go out from Makkah as walking pilgrims, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The riding pilgrim has for every step his mount takes seventy good deeds, and the walking one has for every step seven hundred good deeds."
"12557","12523 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that a muhrim (pilgrim in ihram) was thrown by his mount and died; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his head, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection pronouncing the talbiyah."
"12558","12524 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us (ha). And Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Duhaym narrated to us, saying: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ali al-Azraq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that a muhrim was thrown by his mount and died; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that they wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and not cover his face, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection pronouncing the talbiyah."
"12559","12525 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man among us was thrown upon his mount while in ihram and died; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his face, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection pronouncing the talbiyah."
"12560","12526 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey when a she-camel threw a man and he died while in ihram; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his head or his face, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection pronouncing the talbiyah."
"12561","12527 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ayyash ibn al-Walid al-Raqqam narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Aban ibn Salih, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was traveling, with him a Muslim man in ihram, his camel stumbled with him and he fell from it and was crushed; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in the two garments in which he entered ihram, and do not cover his face, for Allah will resurrect him on the Day of Resurrection chanting the tahlil."
"12562","12528 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hilal ibn Bishr narrated to us, Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, from Umar ibn Amir, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that a man fell from his she-camel; then he mentioned the like of it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"12563","12529 - Isa ibn Muhammad al-Simsar al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: A she-camel threw one of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), killing him while in ihram; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shroud him in his two garments, do not touch him with perfume, wash him with water and lote leaves, and do not cover his face, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection pronouncing the talbiyah."
"12564","12530 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Amr ibn Dinar narrated to him from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that a man was thrown by his camel, crushing him, while in ihram; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Clothe him in two garments, wash him with water and lote leaves, and do not cover his head, for Allah will resurrect him on the Day of Resurrection pronouncing the talbiyah."
"12565","12531 - Abdullah ibn Najiyah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, Hani ibn Sa'id al-Nakha'i narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"12566","12532 - al-Ma'mari and al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Isbahani narrated to us, saying: Maymun ibn al-Asbagh al-Nasibi narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that a man was thrown by his she-camel; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not bring perfume near him, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection pronouncing the talbiyah."
"12567","12533 - Muhammad ibn Fada al-Jawhari al-Basri narrated to us, Ali ibn Muslim al-Tusi narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abu Maryam narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: While a man was upon his she-camel, it threw him and he died; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with lote leaves and water, shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his head or his face, for Allah will resurrect him on the Day of Resurrection pronouncing the talbiyah."
"12568","12534 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Isbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Salih, from Fudayl ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that a muhrim was thrown by his mount; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not bring perfume near him, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection pronouncing the talbiyah - or he said: with matted hair."
"12569","12535 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: A muhrim died in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: Wash him, do not bring near him anything that was forbidden to him, shroud him in his two garments, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection pronouncing the talbiyah."
"12570","12536 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man died while in ihram; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him and shroud him in his two garments, and do not touch him with anything that was forbidden to him, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection pronouncing the talbiyah."
"12571","12537 - Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd al-Bazzaz al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjumanî narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Safwan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: A Muslim man passed away in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he commanded that he be washed and wrapped in two garments, and not be touched with perfume - and I doubt whether his head was covered or not. He said: This one will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection pronouncing the talbiyah."
"12572","12538 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shabib al-Assal al-Isbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and fell from his mount and died; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that he be shrouded and washed, and his face not be covered, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection pronouncing the talbiyah - or he said: chanting the tahlil."
"12573","12539 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My brother was thrown by his camel and died while in ihram; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote leaves and do not embalm him, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection in ihram."
"12574","12540 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: A she-camel threw a muhrim man, killing him, and the Messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached; he said: Wash him and shroud him, do not wash his head, and do not bring perfume near him, for he will be resurrected chanting the tahlil."
"12575","12541 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Matar al-Warraq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man fell from his mount while in ihram and was crushed; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached and it was mentioned to him; he said: Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, do not cover his face, and do not touch him with perfume, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection pronouncing the talbiyah."
"12576","12542 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon a camel while in ihram and it killed him - Shu'bah said: meaning he died - so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments with his head uncovered, and do not touch him with perfume, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection pronouncing the talbiyah."
"12577","12543 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Uthman ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that a man was thrown by his camel and died; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, do not touch him with perfume, and do not cover his head, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection with matted hair."
"12578","12544 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubadah ibn Ziyad al-Asadi narrated to us, Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not know the end of a surah until: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate was revealed to him."
"12579","12545 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji al-Tustari narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us, Fuhayr ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): when: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate was revealed to him, he knew that the surah had ended, and he would begin the next one."
"12580","12546 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Umar ibn Qays, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: Gabriel (peace be upon him) would descend upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with revelation, and when he said: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, he would begin another surah."
"12581","12547 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hawbar ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Warqa, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out of the privy, then sat and ate; they said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not perform ablution? He said: I have only been commanded with ablution for prayer; as for food, no."
"12582","12548 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while in ihram. Thus Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated it, while the companions of al-Thawri narrated it from al-Thawri, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, and that is the correct one."
"12583","12549 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eight combined and five combined, without rain or fear. Thus al-Ju'fi Husayn narrated it from Ibn Uyaynah, while the companions of Ibn Uyaynah narrated it from Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd; and likewise the companions of Amr ibn Dinar narrated it from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd."
"12584","12550 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf and Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh, the two Egyptians, narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi' ibn Umar informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, naked, walking, uncircumcised."
"12585","12551 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abu al-Darda Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Munib al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit and said Amin three times, then said: Do you know why I said Amin? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Gabriel (peace be upon him) came to me and informed me: that whoever is mentioned before you and does not send blessings upon you enters the Fire; may Allah cast him far away and crush him; so I said: Amin. And whoever reaches his parents, or one of them, and does not honor them enters the Fire; may Allah cast him far away and crush him; I said: Amin. And whoever reaches Ramadan and is not forgiven enters the Fire; may Allah cast him far away and crush him; so I said: Amin."
"12586","12552 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abu al-Darda Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Munib narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting one day with people around him, and said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has made for every prophet a desire, and my desire is in standing this night; so let none pray behind me. And Allah has made for every prophet a sustenance portion, and my portion is this fifth; when I am taken, it belongs to those in authority after me."
"12587","12553 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abu al-Darda Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Munib narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated and said: O Allah, bless for us our sa' and our mudd, bless for us our Makkah and our Madinah, bless for us our Syria and our Yemen. A man among the people said: O Prophet of Allah, and our Iraq? He said: In it is the horn of Satan and the howling of tribulations, and harshness is in the East."
"12588","12554 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abu al-Darda Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Munib narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever hears the call and says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger; O Allah, send blessings upon him, grant him the rank of al-Wasilah with You, and place us in his intercession on the Day of Resurrection - intercession becomes due for him."
"12589","12555 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Asim al-Nabil narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, Maslamah ibn Abi Ata narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr who said: Abdullah ibn Abbas and Abdullah ibn Umar testified before me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba, muqayyar, muzaffat, and hantam. I said: What is hantam? He said: All baked clay (vessels)."
"12590","12556 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi, and Abu al-Jarud Mas'ud ibn Muhammad al-Ramli narrated to us, saying: Imran ibn Harun al-Ramli narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Hayyan Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to me, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to me, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, peoples homes through a people and gives them fruitful wealth, though He has not looked at them since He created them out of hatred for them. It was said: How is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Through their joining their kinship ties."
"12591","12557 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim ibn Marzuq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated, then returned and came to the drinking place, and said: Give me to drink of what the people drink."
"12592","12558 - al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and Asr in Madinah without fear."
"12593","12559 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Thabit ibn Abbas Abu Bakr al-Ahdab narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I love you so much that when I remember you, were I not to come and look at you, I would think my soul would depart; then I remember that if I enter Paradise I shall be below you in rank, and that distresses me, and I love to be with you in rank. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not reply anything, so Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: And whoever obeys Allah and the Messenger, those shall be with those whom Allah has blessed - the verse. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and recited it to him."
"12594","12560 - Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke one day and said: Is there any water, is there any water? They said: No. He said: Is there any waterskin? They brought the waterskin, it was placed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he placed his hand upon it, then spread his fingers, and water gushed like the staff of Moses from the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: O Bilal, call the people to ablution. They came performing ablution from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the concern of Ibn Mas'ud was drinking; when they had performed ablution, he led them in the dawn prayer, then sat for the people and said: O people, which of creation has the most wondrous faith? They said: The angels. He said: How should the angels not believe while they witness the matter? They said: Then the prophets, O Messenger of Allah. He said: How should the prophets not believe while revelation descends upon them from heaven? They said: Then your Companions, O Messenger of Allah. He said: How should my Companions not believe while they see what they see? But the most wondrous of people in faith are a people who come after me, believing in me without having seen me, affirming me without having seen me; those are my brothers."
"12595","12561 - Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Naqid al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Samti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj al-Lakhmi narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas who said: A delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: Which of you knows Quss ibn Sa'idah al-Iyadi? They said: All of us, O Messenger of Allah, know him. He said: What happened to him? They said: He perished. He said: I have not forgotten him at Ukaz in the sacred month while he was upon a red camel, addressing the people, saying: O people, gather, listen and heed; whoever lives dies, whoever dies passes away, and all that is coming shall come; in the heaven is news, and in the earth are lessons; a bed laid out, a roof raised, stars moving, seas that never empty; Quss swore a true oath: if there is pleasure in the earth, there shall be displeasure after it; Allah has a religion dearer to Him than your religion upon which you are; why do I see people going and not returning? Were they pleased and so stayed, or were they left and so slept? Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is there among you one who narrates his poetry? One of them recited to him: the generations of the people."
"12596","12562 - Mash ibn Hatim al-Ukli narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Adi narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi who said: I asked Ibn Abbas: Who was the first to accept Islam? He said: Abu Bakr; have you not heard the saying of Hassan ibn Thabit: of mankind."
"12597","12563 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of one who speaks on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon is like a donkey carrying books; and the one who says to him: Be silent - has no Friday."
"12598","12564 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jumhur ibn Mansur narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Mujalid narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas who said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw his Lord, mighty and majestic, twice: once with his sight, and once with his heart."
"12599","12565 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jumhur ibn Mansur narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Mujalid narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas that he used to say regarding His saying: And he saw him at the clear horizon: that he meant Gabriel (peace be upon him); that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him in form at the lote tree of the utmost end."
"12600","12566 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting and in ihram."
